osts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T22:34:40-08:00","id":1179748,"title":"","content":"Well thats annoying. I can't seem to get backerkit to let me see the origins stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T23:01:50-08:00","id":1179759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1179748#post1179748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well thats annoying. I can't seem to get backerkit to let me see the origins stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the problem, exactly? You should be able to click on the Digital Downloads link and download the pdf from there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T23:35:24-08:00","id":1179763,"title":"","content":"Isn\u2019t that just the system preview from last year?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T23:48:16-08:00","id":1179765,"title":"","content":"These are blessed days we live in. Praise the gods for this gift of Scion upon us!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T00:05:58-08:00","id":1179770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1179763#post1179763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn\u2019t that just the system preview from last year?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. It's the complete text of Origin - setting, rules, character creation, combat, antagonists, the whole kaboodle. The Storypath system preview was 34 pages, this is over 200 pages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T00:32:40-08:00","id":1179771,"title":"","content":"They definitely changed the character creation rules a fair amount since the preview, I think I like the New ones quite a bit. I'm really looking forward to the rules for Hero now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2472-trebius","name":"trebius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T02:07:41-08:00","id":1179778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1179759#post1179759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the problem, exactly? You should be able to click on the Digital Downloads link and download the pdf from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not even getting that as a option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T03:26:40-08:00","id":1179782,"title":"","content":"I had trouble finding it too:<br /> <br /> Log onto Backer kit, click on Review Details for the Scion project, this takes you to the survey completion page. The Get Your Digital Download link is at the top of the screen just above &quot;Now its time to thank your project creator&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4972-hurum","name":"hurum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T04:26:50-08:00","id":1179792,"title":"","content":"JUST GOT THE LINK YASS","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T06:16:58-08:00","id":1179806,"title":"","content":"Skimming through, trying to get a grasp on character creation and I'm excited. Already run into a query though: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damage and Scale, p142</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When facing opponents (including objects such as vehicles) of a greater Scale, a character can only deal damage to a target no greater than two Scale above her. For example: A Scion (Scale 0, human-sized) with a sword can slice her way through an armored car (Scale 3), but cannot slash a skyscraper (Scale 5) in half without the aid of a Knack or Boon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this an error, or am I failing to understand something? <br /> <br /> A Scale 0 character is more than 2 Scale below the car, so how are they able to damage it? I can't see anything under the tags for swords that would change it, so it doesn't look like a weapon thing. . <br /> <br /> Looking at the Scale chart, it looks like they've shifted the car up - A car shouldn't be scale 3, even armoured. By size, a <i>bus</i> is Scale 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T06:21:07-08:00","id":1179808,"title":"","content":"Reading through my copy right now and already loving it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T06:46:15-08:00","id":1179813,"title":"","content":"My main question is - well, a bunch of supernatural Paths get Imperfect Disguise as a knack they can take.<br /> <br /> Except there's no benefit to doing so, ever.<br /> <br /> So why do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T07:58:22-08:00","id":1179828,"title":"","content":"So, I was skimming through it (probably won't have the time to properly read it till next weekend sadly) and while I love the altered Character Creation rules and whatever bits I did read, I noticed that there's a God list at the end with all the Gods and their Callings &amp; Purviews.... so looks like Dionysus finally got Liminal, and Brahma and Xi Wang Mu are both Gods now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> !!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T08:32:35-08:00","id":1179836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1179828#post1179828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was skimming through it (probably won't have the time to properly read it till next weekend sadly) and while I love the altered Character Creation rules and whatever bits I did read, I noticed that there's a God list at the end with all the Gods and their Callings &amp; Purviews.... so looks like Dionysus finally got Liminal, and Brahma and Xi Wang Mu are both Gods now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> !!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, divine parents, but still.<br /> <br /> On a similar note, Goibniu and Kali are also listed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T08:46:47-08:00","id":1179840,"title":"","content":"I was reading over the book this morning and was wondering where in the book they talk about the different types of Scions there could be. I remember there being ways a Scion could exist without directly being of their parent's blood. Like Adoption, Mantles, Relics, etc. <br /> <br /> I do see the supernatural path of Saint, but I don't think that is what I am looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T08:51:56-08:00","id":1179841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1179840#post1179840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading over the book this morning and was wondering where in the book they talk about the different types of Scions there could be. I remember there being ways a Scion could exist without directly being of their parent's blood. Like Adoption, Mantles, Relics, etc.<br /> <br /> I do see the supernatural path of Saint, but I don't think that is what I am looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>The different Origins are coming in Hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T08:53:48-08:00","id":1179842,"title":"","content":"I've been going through it and it seems that The Seer was taken out..and maybe Sorcerer as Supernatural Paths...<br /> It even mentions Oracles in the Supernatural Path intro...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3881,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","user":"Mental-Mouse","date":". 01-27-2018, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T10:03:33-08:00","id":1179861,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1344_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1344\" data-vbnamecard=\"1344\">Samudra</a> that is what I thought. Do we have a tentative ETA on Hero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T11:22:04-08:00","id":1179887,"title":"","content":"On backerkit it says soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2472-trebius","name":"trebius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T12:48:42-08:00","id":1179909,"title":"","content":"Live reaction: <br /> <br /> - I'm at page 22 and so far, the chapter does an amazing just of not just explaining, but also <i>conveying</i> how the Divine influences every aspect of the World and how mortals seek to emulate the Gods in order to ride their Legend to something greater. A lot of fictional settings focus on how the Gods treat mortals like cattle -- which isn't necessarily <i>wrong</i>, but I've seen a lot of people get tunnel vision on it at the expense of small things like good worldbuilding and characterization -- so this is something that's unique to Scion for me. I'm also really happy to see it because the idea of Gods and heroes as something mortals aspire too is something I've thought about a few times recently, but not in the context of Scion. <br /> <br /> - The lexicon of different &quot;cults&quot; or whatever you want to call them is very... evocative? It's interesting to know how different people and groups relate to the Gods. <br /> <br /> - I like how dismissive the World is of nitpicking over divergences and plotholes. The premise is that the World is like the world we know, but all myths are real, and players need to accept it and run with it. <br /> <br /> - Hey, there's the rule on learning languages! Always relevant when you're expected to travel the world and hang out with people from different cultures. <br /> <br /> - Is there a meaningful difference between Complicated Stunts and Difficult Stunts? I can kind of see it if I squint a little, but it doesn't seem that big?<br /> <br /> - Giving players the ability to make alterations to a scene based on what the Storyteller gives them is a good idea, but I'm not sure extending that to player's actions is appropriate. If the player are expected to investigate the supernatural problems of the World, I think it's important to encourage preparation <i>before</i> an encounter. Could just be a matter of personal preference though. <br /> <br /> - Are all the Gods' Callings listed somewhere, since we need to know them to pick a pre-Visitation Scion's Calling? I guess I'll find out eventually. <br /> <br /> - Heroic Knacks are (apparently) in Origin. That's cool for the preview. <br /> <br /> - The section on Contacts, invocation and their dots is a little confusing and I'd rather move on with the text than try to parse it out at the moment. I may come back to it later. <br /> <br /> - Some of the Paths list a Command skill, but I think it should be Leadership? And was there an Enigmas skill? I can't remember. <br /> <br /> - Mandatory Highlander reference is mandatory. <br /> <br /> - The mortal Knacks are surprisingly good. What do Hero-tier Knacks look like?<br /> <br /> - And another language ability. <br /> <br /> - Seriously though, these are hella practical, even if they're not necessarily powerful. I really want to know how Hero Knacks compete. <br /> <br /> - Skipping combat. It can't be that important, can it?<br /> <br /> - Storyguiding... maybe important? <br /> <br /> - The advice on how to craft stories with mythical motifs is useful. <br /> <br /> - Does the Virtue track change every single time you do something that represents one Virtue and not the other? Because that seems very swingy.<br /> <br /> - And there's the list of Callings and Purviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T12:59:48-08:00","id":1179913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1179840#post1179840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading over the book this morning and was wondering where in the book they talk about the different types of Scions there could be. I remember there being ways a Scion could exist without directly being of their parent's blood. Like Adoption, Mantles, Relics, etc.<br /> <br /> I do see the supernatural path of Saint, but I don't think that is what I am looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was looking for that too. I think it's been incorporated into the Origin Path options, where the examples include things like <i>Chosen </i>and <i>Created</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","name":"Not Quite Yoda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T14:09:51-08:00","id":1179932,"title":"","content":"Is there a character sheet somewhere to be able to try the character creation process from this pdf? I mean it's hard to visualize without one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23785-vonigner","name":"vonigner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T15:17:07-08:00","id":1179950,"title":"","content":"I just started reading, and I definitely like how they keep plenty of metaphorical doors wide open to use later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T15:52:48-08:00","id":1179959,"title":"","content":"Hm, I admit on the Knacks I'm a bit curious.<br /> <br /> Earlier it says that Knacks require Momentum, but some of the Knacks seem to imply they're always active, if conditional. And there's a couple that seem to be designed on the assumption that they don't cost Momentum, such as &quot;Born to be Kings&quot;, which says &quot;The first time each scene the Scion would add one Momentum to the Black Pool, they add 2 instead&quot;. Because in the case of &quot;All Knacks Cost Momentum&quot;, then Born to be Kings is literally useless. Like, you spend a Momentum to activate it, and the first time you would add Momentum you add <b>2</b>... But you've already spent one momentum to activate the Knack so you've added a net 1 Momentum to the pool which you would have done without the Knack.<br /> <br /> Is this a case where SOME Knacks require Momentum and will tell you if they do? Or were some of these written before the &quot;All Knacks Cost Momentum&quot; rule and need to be reconsidered?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T16:10:21-08:00","id":1179965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1179909#post1179909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The section on Contacts, invocation and their dots is a little confusing and I'd rather move on with the text than try to parse it out at the moment. I may come back to it later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was trying to make a character, and that bit was a real puzzler. It seems like every time you invoke a specific contact, they get more dots and more tags, but I'm not sure whether that's right and, if it is, if that persists between sessions. It makes it seem like a game would end up with a list of five-dot contacts who all end up somewhat similar unless you invent new tags pretty often, if so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23646-goblinsociety","name":"GoblinSociety","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T16:40:52-08:00","id":1179973,"title":"","content":"Really loved the text so far, but I did have a couple of questions:<br /> <br /> Several places mention the dots assigned to your calling improving their associated knacks, but there is no mention of raising the level of your calling in character advancement. What is the max it can be raised to, and how do you do it? Is it the same cost as a skill?<br /> <br /> The other thing i noticed is the character creation rules state that skills cannot be repeated in your starting paths more than twice, but the starting example of Little Mao has Culture in all 3 paths. Is this intentional?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","name":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T17:12:05-08:00","id":1179983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1179959#post1179959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, I admit on the Knacks I'm a bit curious.<br /> <br /> Earlier it says that Knacks require Momentum, but some of the Knacks seem to imply they're always active, if conditional. And there's a couple that seem to be designed on the assumption that they don't cost Momentum, such as &quot;Born to be Kings&quot;, which says &quot;The first time each scene the Scion would add one Momentum to the Black Pool, they add 2 instead&quot;. Because in the case of &quot;All Knacks Cost Momentum&quot;, then Born to be Kings is literally useless. Like, you spend a Momentum to activate it, and the first time you would add Momentum you add <b>2</b>... But you've already spent one momentum to activate the Knack so you've added a net 1 Momentum to the pool which you would have done without the Knack.<br /> <br /> Is this a case where SOME Knacks require Momentum and will tell you if they do? Or were some of these written before the &quot;All Knacks Cost Momentum&quot; rule and need to be reconsidered?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all Knacks require Momentum. Only a few do. I'll mark that as a text clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T17:14:12-08:00","id":1179984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1179983#post1179983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all Knacks require Momentum. Only a few do. I'll mark that as a text clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, that would be wonderful. If I could recommend, perhaps a line like &quot;Some Knacks require the spending of Momentum&quot; in appropriate places under the &quot;Knack Costs&quot; section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T17:27:42-08:00","id":1179989,"title":"","content":"Does the Sage knack Blockade of Reason do anything for unvisited scions? It says it protects you against people of lower tiers, but I thought regular mortals and unvisited scions were on the same tier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2472-trebius","name":"trebius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T18:28:25-08:00","id":1180003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1179836#post1179836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, divine parents, but still.<br /> <br /> On a similar note, Goibniu and Kali are also listed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed! On the other side of things, though, Danu and Osanyin seem to have decided this book is a little passe and have gone off to do other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T18:50:04-08:00","id":1180006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trebius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1179989#post1179989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Sage knack Blockade of Reason do anything for unvisited scions? It says it protects you against people of lower tiers, but I thought regular mortals and unvisited scions were on the same tier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, with Blockade of Reason, supernatural lies would still trigger a Clash of Wills, with a decent Enhancement bonus. That could potentially shut down a lot of Trickster type Knacks.<br /> <br /> There are similar situations for Hunter Apex Predator and Judge Lie Detector Knacks at the Origin level, but they don't even get that. So, yeah, don't take them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 01-27-2018, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T21:03:12-08:00","id":1180054,"title":"","content":"I wonder how Guides work at the Origin level. Like, if you were fostered by an Incarnation or Scion of the Tuatha, are they a Connection that gets upgraded to a Guide after the visitation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T00:39:05-08:00","id":1180092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180054#post1180054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how Guides work at the Origin level. Like, if you were fostered by an Incarnation or Scion of the Tuatha, are they a Connection that gets upgraded to a Guide after the visitation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming Guide is still a birthright, yeah? You pick either 2 Knacks or 4 Birthrights in the Finishing Touches of character creation, so you might just get the straight up guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T01:02:07-08:00","id":1180095,"title":"","content":"Is it me, or are PCs going to get hurt, like, a lot? A beat cop, the lowest combat threat presented, is rolling 5 dice to attack. PCs are rolling 5 dice, at most, to defend - probably less considering not every PC is going to max a resilience stat. That's a low-end mook? Someone who is going to hit most PCs most of the time? I realize you're probably going to wipe them out in your own attack as well, but Attack of Attribute + Skill against Defense of Attribute feels incredibly unbalanced towards offense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T02:40:12-08:00","id":1180106,"title":"","content":"Well, armor is a thing one should not forget","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23677-the-eternal-keeper","name":"The Eternal Keeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T03:04:17-08:00","id":1180111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180095#post1180095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it me, or are PCs going to get hurt, like, a lot? A beat cop, the lowest combat threat presented, is rolling 5 dice to attack. PCs are rolling 5 dice, at most, to defend - probably less considering not every PC is going to max a resilience stat. That's a low-end mook? Someone who is going to hit most PCs most of the time? I realize you're probably going to wipe them out in your own attack as well, but Attack of Attribute + Skill against Defense of Attribute feels incredibly unbalanced towards offense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's already reminding me of Aberrant, where if you didn't win initiative, you spend your turn defending because otherwise the character who went first was going to wipe the other out in a single blow. It's not that swingy, but it's definitely tilted to offence.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23677-the-eternal-keeper\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23677\" data-vbnamecard=\"23677\">The Eternal Keeper</a> - I'm not sure armour is hugely significant.<br /> <br /> For one thing, I'm not convinced it's practical to wear it openly at the mortal level. If you're wandering around wearing armour, you're going to get stopped by the police, people aren't going to be willing to talk to you, and it's just going to make everything harder. It's obtrusive in a way that a hidden gun or a sword in a dufflebag isn't. It screams &quot;I'm about to get into a fight&quot;. Now, that can be countered by the Concealable tag, but it does limit the armour you can wear. My read is that [Concealable][Soft] armour is probably going to be the default, which raises the difficulty to damage you by 1.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, while that's generally <i>really good</i> (At mortal level, that's roughly equivalent to 3 extra defence dice, and will entirely negate the defensive deficit), it's entirely countered if that beat cop uses his [Piercing] handgun. So maybe [Concealable][Hard] should be the default, because it means you can safely take one bullet per combat without taking injuries.<br /> <br /> Also, big question here: Are Pre-Visitation Scions mortal for the purposes of Lethal damage? The book uses &quot;Mortal&quot; to refer to both the Tier (Which Pre-Visitation Scions are) and the state of not being descended from Gods (Which Pre-Visitation Scions clearly <i>aren't</i>). And Origins includes things like &quot;Mortal Sorcerers&quot; as character options, and they clearly <i>are</i> mortals in both senses of the word.<br /> <br /> Because if Origins player characters are mortals for the purposes of Lethal damage, then they're going to be taking Persistent conditions from Lethal damage, which they can't get rid of. And handguns bypass Bruised entirely, so they're going straight onto your Injured or Maimed boxes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hmm. I'd have to see how often Weighty comes up, because<br /> <br /> Kevlar Vest: Soft (1), Concealable, Resistant (Bulletproof), Weighty<br /> <br /> is very good. A beat cop, rolling 5 dice is looking at needing an above average roll to hurt you even without counting in your defence (Soft armour means that to inflict an injury, you're needing 2 successes total over your defence, and he averages less than a single success). With just 3 dice in your defence (I.e. an average of a single success) you're not quite untouchable to the mooks, but you're not in too much danger from just a couple of beat cops.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait, the Kevlar vest is given as an example, but it's not legal, is it? Soft [1], Concealable [2]. Resistant [2], Weighty [-1]. Total of [4], which is too many tag points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2649,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","user":"Tarion","date":". 01-28-2018, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T03:35:41-08:00","id":1180115,"title":"","content":"Is it intentional that some pantheons completely lack a specific calling?<br /> <br /> For example, the Tuatha completely lack the Hunter calling, and the Asir lack Healer... which I discovered because those were my first two character concepts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T04:49:49-08:00","id":1180123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180115#post1180115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it intentional that some pantheons completely lack a specific calling?<br /> <br /> For example, the Tuatha completely lack the Hunter calling, and the Asir lack Healer... which I discovered because those were my first two character concepts...</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be just a side-effect of the actual mythology... are there any major Hunter figures in Tuatha myth that could serve as a patron? It might also simply be that they couldn't fit in every possible God with every Calling in the core book... Idun would probably be the Aesir Healer (or at least an Aesir with the Healer Calling), she's just not written up right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T05:38:14-08:00","id":1180133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180123#post1180123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Might be just a side-effect of the actual mythology... are there any major Hunter figures in Tuatha myth that could serve as a patron? It might also simply be that they couldn't fit in every possible God with every Calling in the core book... Idun would probably be the Aesir Healer (or at least an Aesir with the Healer Calling), she's just not written up right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Paramedic Scion of Idun was one of my original concepts before this PDF came out, so I definitely agree with you there. Though I'm not as familiar with the Tuatha, off the top of my head, perhaps The Morrigan could get Hunter... I know that she already has 3, but it's not like they stuck to only 3 per god... (Nana\u2019B\u2019Oozoo has only 2, while Freyja has 4)... but if you really wanted to stick to 3, I'm really not seeing how Sage fits her any better then Hunter might (At the Heroic level at least)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T06:02:56-08:00","id":1180141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180133#post1180133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Paramedic Scion of Idun was one of my original concepts before this PDF came out, so I definitely agree with you there. Though I'm not as familiar with the Tuatha, off the top of my head, perhaps The Morrigan could get Hunter... I know that she already has 3, but it's not like they stuck to only 3 per god... (Nana\u2019B\u2019Oozoo has only 2, while Freyja has 4)... but if you really wanted to stick to 3, I'm really not seeing how Sage fits her any better then Hunter might (At the Heroic level at least)...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty certain those two are either errors or have something especially weird going on, cuz as far as I am aware each God is <i>supposed</i> to have only Three Callings. As for Morrigan having Sage, I'm no Tuatha expert but doesn't she have associations with Prophecy? Sage has Prophetic powers, I think, so she may have it for that. I also found her lack of Warrior weird, but this is a question for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> : Does the Morrigan ever actually fight or she an example of a War Goddess who's not a Warrior Goddess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T06:16:54-08:00","id":1180146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180141#post1180141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty certain those two are either errors or have something especially weird going on, cuz as far as I am aware each God is <i>supposed</i> to have only Three Callings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I thought so too, but then I read the PDF and I began to wonder if the &quot;Rule&quot; was merely a &quot;Guideline&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180141#post1180141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Morrigan having Sage, I'm no Tuatha expert but doesn't she have associations with Prophecy? Sage has Prophetic powers, I think, so she may have it for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Sage has no Prophetic powers whatsoever at the Heroic level. On the other hand Liminal does, and she has that. Liminal, Lover, and Sage are her 3 Callings. The Morrigan is Inevitable, run from her all you want, try and avoid her all you can, but in the end, she will find you... and that just screams hunter to me...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180141#post1180141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also found her lack of Warrior weird, but this is a question for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> : Does the Morrigan ever actually fight or she an example of a War Goddess who's not a Warrior Goddess?</div> </div> </div> </div>I too found that weird. I expected Liminal, Hunter and Warrior to be her callings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T06:45:51-08:00","id":1180152,"title":"","content":"Morrigan's mythology is kinda messy. What the best three are is going to depend highly on which take on her (or them) you go with.<br /> <br /> The problem with Hunter and Warrior as far as I can tell is that she doesn't generally join in the battle or stalk people. Her war association is more because of her giving of omens and portends around death - especially violent death - than her being a particularly noteworthy combatant.<br /> <br /> It's possible that some of the assignments just make more sense once we start seeing the Hero level Knacks. Master of the World (esp. a more supernatural upgrade of it) being a Sage Knack is the sort of thing I'd expect of a goddess that influences the outcomes of battles. Palace of Memory ramped up to post-cognition levels, and Office Hours via signs and portents to give generals help in making battle plans all seem to be well within her wheelhouse. So there's a solid case for Sage here.<br /> <br /> Lover is the one I struggle with. The general concept of Lover as denoting a godess that can inflame emotions isn't necessarily a bad fit for some of the ways she's been described, but the Lover Knacks all hinge more on positive stuff, where most of what would make sense in this take on her is in the Leader Knacks like Cloak of Dread (she's feared as an omen of death), Good Listener (overlapping with the case for Sage in knowing stuff), Grand Entrance (again with being such a strong portent just appearing on the battlefield is supposed to matter), and Perfect Poise (OK, probably a weak example as the first half of the Knack makes sense and the second less so).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T07:08:38-08:00","id":1180156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180146#post1180146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I thought so too, but then I read the PDF and I began to wonder if the &quot;Rule&quot; was merely a &quot;Guideline&quot;.<br /> <br /> No. Sage has no Prophetic powers whatsoever at the Heroic level. On the other hand Liminal does, and she has that. Liminal, Lover, and Sage are her 3 Callings. The Morrigan is Inevitable, run from her all you want, try and avoid her all you can, but in the end, she will find you... and that just screams hunter to me...<br /> <br /> I too found that weird. I expected Liminal, Hunter and Warrior to be her callings.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180141#post1180141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty certain those two are either errors or have something especially weird going on, cuz as far as I am aware each God is <i>supposed</i> to have only Three Callings. As for Morrigan having Sage, I'm no Tuatha expert but doesn't she have associations with Prophecy? Sage has Prophetic powers, I think, so she may have it for that. I also found her lack of Warrior weird, but this is a question for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> : Does the Morrigan ever actually fight or she an example of a War Goddess who's not a Warrior Goddess?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been summoned. Right, what's goin' on? Oh, The Morr\u00edgan? Right.<br /> <br /> I think Liminal, Lover, and Sage perfectly encompass The Morr\u00edgan in a merged form.<ul><li><b>Liminal </b>is obviously there due to her function as a spooky, something-to-do-with-the-dead-but-we-don't-actually-know-what, and mysterious function. The Scene in the Boyhood Deeds where Badb helps C\u00faChulainn kill a spectre tie into this (since this form of The Morr\u00edgan is a merged entity as I will get to in a moment).</li> <li><b>Sage </b>I think is also very important due to The Morr\u00edgan's function as a knowledge source, helping the Tuatha De Danann during Cath Maige Tuired with information, as well as her stated skills with magic as she levies various sorts of odd curses upon the Fomorians during Cath Maige Tuired. Furthermore, while Sage lacks support for Prophetic Powers at <i>Hero</i>, that doesn't mean it lacks it at Demigod, or God. I would argue that Sage likely is intended to be used for Prophetic functions based on other people who have Sage. Apollo, for instance, is a totally useless adviser, but does hold an Oracular function represented by his Sage Calling. Dionysus also has Sage, and he's not very good at advice outside of his function as a Mystery Cult Patron, and thus we see Sage being tied back into this notion of spontaneous divine knowledge. Amaterasu has Sage due to the Oracular contest with her brother Susano-Wo, Hachiman has a function as a foretell victory with... doves IIRC, it's been a while since the Kami revision and I'm up to my eyes in Teutates currently. For the Tuatha specifically, The Dagda also has been given Sage with obviously is tying into his function as a source of Otherworldly Knowledge, so, yeah. I think it is safe to assume that while Sage may currently not support Oracular functions at Hero, probably does at higher Legends. So, I would say Sage is really solid for her.<ul><li>Subcomment: If you have read Cath Maige Tuired and don't remember The Morr\u00edgan giving two really big prophecies, that's because they are something called <i>rosc</i> passages and are the most horrific, hellish thing in the world to translate. Cath Maige Tuired has three IIRC, two of her prophecies, and then there is one describing the fight between Balor and Lug. They are cryptic to the point of no successful well thought of translation from the original manuscript text existing. While we don't know the exact words, we do know that The Morr\u00edgan is giving a prophecy of some sort in these passages, and they appear to be incredibly dire ones.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Lover</b>: So, Lover is really important for The Morr\u00edgan in this merged state since she has merged with Macha as evidenced by the presence of Beasts (Horses) and Epic Dexterity. The story of Macha and her mortal husband is a perfect story of a Lover, she shows up one day, takes over his household, decides she's married to him. Very Irish conceptualization of this sort of thing. In addition to Macha, I would argue that The Morr\u00edgan herself (the singular entity named The Morr\u00edgan, not the group entity) has the entire scene with C\u00faChulainn which is seemingly intentionally connected with the same sort of interaction we see between himself, L\u00ed Ban, and Fand in The Sickbed of C\u00faChulainn. She is spurned by C\u00faChulainn since her request is that he abandon his post and run off with her, also because he's sort of busy when she accosts him, but it is a very Lover feeling scene. Then you have the whole thing with The Dagda on top of that. So, Lover I'd consider almost foundational to the character.</li> <li><b>Hunter</b>: The Morr\u00edgan doesn't really... do anything like this. She doesn't spend time in the wilderness (the Tuatha are actually way more into clearcutting forest and leveling natural wilderness for use as pastoral lands than people give them credit for) and doesn't track anyone down at any point. I know in popular culture there is an idea of her being a Psychopomp, or a Death-Source, but it sadly unfounded in the Saga literature. So, Hunter doesn't actually have any basis in myth.</li> <li><b>Warrior</b>: Also another pop-culture misunderstanding. The Morr\u00edgan doesn't really fight, that's not her thing. She takes part in... I think one fight, but that does not make her a warrior like Lug, Ogma, etc. She is involved during warfare against the Fomorians, but mostly through strange magical functions such as the theft of the... what was it, courage of the liver? Something odd. The Morr\u00edgan herself is not a divine fighter, she is not there in the thick of it clashing with others, she is using strange magic, and influencing combat, but not partaking directly in any degree that would justify putting her on the same level as individuals who take more of a major role in fighting. She's got a chariot, but everyone in the Tuatha has a chariot, status thing. She helps in battle, but that's because literally all of the Tuatha help in battles. Cultural thing.</li> </ul>So yeah, I'd say The Morr\u00edgan as presented is a solid entry. If she was broken up into her component parts she might have some different Callings perhaps? I can see Macha with Sage (Curse of Macha), Lover (explained above), and Creator (Mother function) for instance. Ultimately however, the rules are guidelines in any game. I don't think I would give The Morr\u00edgan Hunter or Warrior in any of my games since I don't think there's any proof of such a function in the Saga texts, but if other people want to do so, that's totally reasonable. Do whatever makes the game fun for you.<br /> <br /> About the general absence of Hunter with the Tuatha I can explain though. So, your legal and social status in early medieval / older Ireland was dependent on your tribe, and being inside your tribal lands. If, for instance, a Smith from Ulster was in Munster, they would have no legal status, and no social status. Forests, and other wilderness areas are therefore beyond the law, beyond <i>status</i>, and <i>that</i> is fundamentally important for the Irish at the time. Being a hunter, living off hunted game, would be one of the lowest status social ranks, below even someone who is a herder. You would have almost no social standing, respect, power, or legal status. This is seen with the Fianna, bands of young warrior nobles who lived in the woods to more-or-less work off the testosterone in a way that wouldn't damage the tribe, sort of. These Fianna bands were half-outlaw, half-helpful, raiding both their own communities, and outsider ones. They are hunters, they are people in the wilderness, and until they return home and become actual members of society, they held a very nebulious position in the social system. The only people who had any 'mobile' social status were the Fili, or the classes that spawned off of them as they seemingly broke up or decayed into separate groups, such as the bards. Everyone else needed to stay within their tribe, or lose everything that mattered.<br /> <br /> So, that's why Hunter is probably not represented very well in the Pantheon. There are certainly Irish characters who would have Hunter, Finn being the big one, but none of the Tuatha themselves short of nameless ones in the background since their numbers outclass the stars in the sky, waves in the sea, grains of sand, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T07:35:46-08:00","id":1180160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180092#post1180092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm assuming Guide is still a birthright, yeah? You pick either 2 Knacks or 4 Birthrights in the Finishing Touches of character creation, so you might just get the straight up guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I must have glossed over that part or forgotten about it since Birthrights aren't in the Origins text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T08:30:08-08:00","id":1180170,"title":"","content":"In the Paths section, it says that you can\u2019t take the same skill in all three paths, but the sample character (Little Mao) does just that with Culture.<br /> <br /> Also, it says that you have to take both on your pantheon\u2019s Skills in connection with your Society Path, but Little Mao doesn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Clarification?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T09:48:58-08:00","id":1180190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagardner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180170#post1180170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Paths section, it says that you can\u2019t take the same skill in all three paths, but the sample character (Little Mao) does just that with Culture.<br /> <br /> Also, it says that you have to take both on your pantheon\u2019s Skills in connection with your Society Path, but Little Mao doesn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Clarification?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've flagged that for correction. You can choose the same Skill for all three Paths, you just can't have a Skill that goes over 5, so you need to redistribute your dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T12:16:04-08:00","id":1180219,"title":"","content":"Expanding on that, on page 104 in the bullet section it says &quot;Any given Skill can be associated with at most two of your Paths&quot; while on the following page (105) at the end of the first paragraph it says &quot;If this gives a Skill more than three dots, redistribute the extra dot to another Path Skill.&quot;<br /> <br /> I get what you're saying Neall, just wanted to make sure that all of it gets corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T14:14:57-08:00","id":1180246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180156#post1180156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the general absence of Hunter with the Tuatha I can explain though. So, your legal and social status in early medieval / older Ireland was dependent on your tribe, and being inside your tribal lands. If, for instance, a Smith from Ulster was in Munster, they would have no legal status, and no social status. Forests, and other wilderness areas are therefore beyond the law, beyond <i>status</i>, and <i>that</i> is fundamentally important for the Irish at the time. Being a hunter, living off hunted game, would be one of the lowest status social ranks, below even someone who is a herder. You would have almost no social standing, respect, power, or legal status. This is seen with the Fianna, bands of young warrior nobles who lived in the woods to more-or-less work off the testosterone in a way that wouldn't damage the tribe, sort of. These Fianna bands were half-outlaw, half-helpful, raiding both their own communities, and outsider ones. They are hunters, they are people in the wilderness, and until they return home and become actual members of society, they held a very nebulious position in the social system. The only people who had any 'mobile' social status were the Fili, or the classes that spawned off of them as they seemingly broke up or decayed into separate groups, such as the bards. Everyone else needed to stay within their tribe, or lose everything that mattered.<br /> <br /> So, that's why Hunter is probably not represented very well in the Pantheon. There are certainly Irish characters who would have Hunter, Finn being the big one, but none of the Tuatha themselves short of nameless ones in the background since their numbers outclass the stars in the sky, waves in the sea, grains of sand, etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey Watcher, thank you for helping me understand the Morrigan better. I will accept your judgement on that matter of her Callings because it's obvious that you know her far better then I, but I take exception to the above. Not because you are wrong, about any of it, but because the so called &quot;Hunter&quot; calling has, at least at Mortal Tier, nothing to do with the living, or being, in the wilderness, and everything to do with, and this is a direct quote, &quot;pursuit and perception&quot;. A detective tracking a perp, a bounty hunter and his prey, a vigilante hunting his wife's killer, and a cyber security specialist routing out a hacker are all valid uses of the Hunter Knacks. The fact that they can also be used to hunt game in the wild, is at most secondary. Now I'll freely admit that I haven't seen Heroic thru God Tier Knacks, and things might look very differently once we do, however, until we do, I see nothing wrong with any Pantheon having at least 1 God with access to any given Calling, Tuatha included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T15:58:51-08:00","id":1180270,"title":"","content":"&quot;Titanic Scions are mortals caged in raw Purviews, forced to look at the World through alien eyes and a human mind&quot;<br /> <br /> I like that we have some talk on what Titanic Scions are like, but I'm trying to figure out what this means in simpler words. What would someone who is a Scion of...Prometheus or Helios experience the world like I guess? This is a really evocative line that doesn't explain much to me which is eating me up because I have an idea of a Titanic Scion villain in my game and want to make sure what I have in my head would fit thematically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T16:12:40-08:00","id":1180273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180246#post1180246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Watcher, thank you for helping me understand the Morrigan better. I will accept your judgement on that matter of her Callings because it's obvious that you know her far better then I, but I take exception to the above. Not because you are wrong, about any of it, but because the so called &quot;Hunter&quot; calling has, at least at Mortal Tier, nothing to do with the living, or being, in the wilderness, and everything to do with, and this is a direct quote, &quot;pursuit and perception&quot;. A detective tracking a perp, a bounty hunter and his prey, a vigilante hunting his wife's killer, and a cyber security specialist routing out a hacker are all valid uses of the Hunter Knacks. The fact that they can also be used to hunt game in the wild, is at most secondary. Now I'll freely admit that I haven't seen Heroic thru God Tier Knacks, and things might look very differently once we do, however, until we do, I see nothing wrong with any Pantheon having at least 1 God with access to any given Calling, Tuatha included.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am absolutely happy to help! If you ever want to know stuff about the Tuatha, I can help out here or there! I am a wealth of borderline useless information that only helps with Scion, and my thesis. I am always really happy to get a chance to teach people about the Irish Saga texts. It's one of my favorite things in the world.<br /> <br /> I'm unsure which of the major Tuatha fits closest with Hunter's notion of perception or pursuit. The closest I can think is Aengus for trying to track down Etain, but he needs so much help with it I think that almost disqualifies him from it. I expect you want a Divine Parent with it due to the limitation of having to pick one of your Divine Parent's callings? That's a pretty good point I hadn't thought about. I initially thought you meant each Pantheon from their base Deities should have each Calling represented, but you mean that there should be a selection of figures to make sure everything's represented, that makes absolute sense.<br /> <br /> I obviously can't reach out and change the game, but hey, I build houserule documents all the time. From what we have been shown from the Backerkit, I could whip up a Calling and Purview List of someone who would have Hunter from the Irish Sagas if you'd like one! They might be really minor, but hey, I've got a lot of books sitting around me, could put'm to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T16:31:00-08:00","id":1180280,"title":"","content":"Probably best to take a notably missing Purview or Calling in a Pantheon as a potential niche for your PC to potentially grow to fill!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T16:55:13-08:00","id":1180287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180273#post1180273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect you want a Divine Parent with it due to the limitation of having to pick one of your Divine Parent's callings?</div> </div> </div> </div> Got it in one. It wouldn't be as much of an issue at the Heroic Tier, but at Mortal, you only get one Calling, and if Hunter fits my character best, then I cannot be descended from the Tuatha. I could always pick something else, like Liminal, or Warrior, and pick up Hunter at Heroic Tier, but they don't fit the character as well, and that sucks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180273#post1180273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a pretty good point I hadn't thought about. I initially thought you meant each Pantheon from their base Deities should have each Calling represented, but you mean that there should be a selection of figures to make sure everything's represented, that makes absolute sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am definitely looking at it from a &quot;players wanting to make characters&quot; perspective. I'm not stuck on any one particular god having any given Calling, I just feel that if I want to play a Mortal Tier character, I should have at least 1 option for each Calling amongst any given pantheon.<br /> <br /> Is there any one that had a notable quest/oath to slay someone/thing? Or perhaps someone that swore vengeance, or retribution, someone who went to great lengths to get it? Recovering an item that was stolen by tracking down the one that took it. Those sorts of things are all covered under the Hunter Calling. (IMNSHO, The Punisher would have the Hunter Calling if he were a Mortal Scion of some pantheon)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180273#post1180273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I obviously can't reach out and change the game, but hey, I build houserule documents all the time. From what we have been shown from the Backerkit, I could whip up a Calling and Purview List of someone who would have Hunter from the Irish Sagas if you'd like one! They might be really minor, but hey, I've got a lot of books sitting around me, could put'm to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who is an Norse/Irish mix (Heavy on the Norse), I'm far more familiar with the Asir mythology then the Tuatha, and I would greatly appreciate any help you would be willing to give on the matter. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T17:25:52-08:00","id":1180294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180111#post1180111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's already reminding me of Aberrant, where if you didn't win initiative, you spend your turn defending because otherwise the character who went first was going to wipe the other out in a single blow. It's not that swingy, but it's definitely tilted to offence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with Aberrant, so I can't comment on similarities. But with NPCs and PCs using different rules for defending (PC defense is rolled, while NPC defense is a static difficulty that the attacker needs to overcome), NPCs don't have an option to use full defense - instead, the size of their defense values look like it's assumed that they're automatically full defending, but can still act. They also don't take injury conditions. So, basically, unless they get taken out entirely or are hit by something that causes a condition other than damage, they both attack and defend at full capacity.<br /> <br /> It might actually be to many characters' benefit to go last, so they know if they need to full defend or not in any given round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T18:11:03-08:00","id":1180300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180287#post1180287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any one that had a notable quest/oath to slay someone/thing? Or perhaps someone that swore vengeance, or retribution, someone who went to great lengths to get it? Recovering an item that was stolen by tracking down the one that took it. Those sorts of things are all covered under the Hunter Calling. (IMNSHO, The Punisher would have the Hunter Calling if he were a Mortal Scion of some pantheon)<br /> <br /> As someone who is an Norse/Irish mix (Heavy on the Norse), I'm far more familiar with the Asir mythology then the Tuatha, and I would greatly appreciate any help you would be willing to give on the matter. Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a <i>ton</i> of people who have vengeance driven tasks to murder another person, sadly, mostly mortals. And the one time Lug does it he does it through the most trickster-y way possible that means he actually puts in like zero effort in the actual searching, and tricks the wrongdoers into getting themselves killed. It's a weird myth. Lug and The Dagda also have to go find The Dagda's harp one time, but it's less of a search and more of kicking in a door, threatening some Fomorians, and walking out. No searching or anything involved.<br /> <br /> I do, however, have very unorthodox basis for the Hunter Calling to offer up to you.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Midir</b> </span><span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Pronounced: Mithir)</span><br /> Proud, devious, and cruel at times, Midir the king of S\u00edd Br\u00ed L\u00e9ith, is one of the more confusing members of the Tribes of the Goddess Danu. He flits in and out of the stories, sometimes replacing a better known figure for a single retelling, only to vanish the next time. He has been The Dagda's father, his brother, and son, as well as the father of Macha, Ailbe, and Dorind at times. He is a wealthy man, happy to use his great wealth to acomplish whatever whim he has at the time, and while he has been a kind, benevolent foster-father to Aengus Og, he can fall to a furious black rage when wronged one too many times, bringing dread with his arrival at Tara when Eochaid had married a reincarnation of his love \u00c9ta\u00edn as he arrived in his full might and anger as Eochaid had the audacity to split open S\u00edd mounds in a search for \u00c9ta\u00edn when she had been stolen away. He also had his primary wife, F\u00faammnach, killed by Aengus Og when she was seeking to kill \u00c9ta\u00edn. His love for \u00c9ta\u00edn defines him, though this love is tainted to a degree, exercising a concerning amount of control over her, even in the context of the time. However, he seems to have calmed down over time to the point that \u00c9ta\u00edn herself begins taking mortal lovers such as Eochaid Feidlech. (a different one than the Eochaid Midir clashed with)<br /> <br /> He once owned the cauldron of The Dagda, though it was stolen away from him by C\u00faChulainn, and once owned three cranes of stinginess, though they were stolen by the mortal satirist Athairne Ailgesach. He provided a magical horse to Eochu mac Maireda and R\u00edb at one point, though the creature was rather... cunning in of itself, urinating to much in a great thundering stream that it created Lough Ree. Midir has died, like most of the people of the Goddess Danu, killed by Elcmar, who was then killed by Aengus Og. However, death hasn't stopped the Pantheon from meddling long after their deaths.<ul><li><b>Callings</b><ul><li><b>Hunter</b>: His search for \u00c9ta\u00edn takes Midir thousands of years, and despite that he never gives up his search. He is capable of recognizing \u00c9ta\u00edn when she has been transformed into a giant fly by Midir's primary wife (the Irish practiced polygamy with a 'primary wife' system) F\u00faammnach. Is willing to go to great lengths, pay massive prices, and cause others to commit colossal socitial violations to get his prize.</li> <li><b>Lover</b>: Midir's largest myth, <i>Tochmarc \u00c9ta\u00edne</i> (which you can read <a href=\"http://www.maryjones.us/ctexts/etain.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>!), is the story of his adoration for the woman \u00c9ta\u00edn, chasing her through a thousand years, and different reincarnations, loving her even when she was a giant (albeit very useful) fly. Willing to do horrible things for love.</li> <li><b>Trickster</b>: Midir accomplishes his goals through manipulating, tricking, and decieving others. In his final gambit to win \u00c9ta\u00edn from her most recent husband Eochaid, he not only uses a word ploy to steal \u00c9ta\u00edn from him, but then in an act of furious vengeance, tricks Eochaid into having a child with his own daughter with \u00c9ta\u00edn after tricking him into thinking the daughter was \u00c9ta\u00edn. (This is a <i>very big deal</i> in Ireland, they don't like incest at all)</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Purviews</b><ul><li><b>Deception</b>: Magically tricks Ailill into falling into a Wasting Sickness for \u00c9ta\u00edn so he can disguise himself as him to sleep with her, may have been the source of Aengus Og's trick to take the Brug from Elcmar (probably Nuadu). His final lie to Eochaid is really rather complex, and results in Eochaid committing the large taboo of incest.</li> <li><b>Order</b>: Midir is the R\u00edg (chief / king) of Br\u00ed L\u00e9ith (modernly known as Ardagh Hill, Co. Cork. You can see it <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/maps/place/Ardagh+Hill,+Ardagh,+Unionhall,+Co.+Cork,+Ireland/@51.5598221,-9.1465602,499m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m13!1m7!3m6!1s0x4845ae97fe27e72f:0xa9ae4675984e5e46!2sArdagh+Hill,+Ardagh,+Unionhall,+Co.+Cork,+Ireland!3b1!8m2!3d51.5593202!4d-9.1449504!3m4!1s0x4845ae97fe27e72f:0xa9ae4675984e5e46!8m2!3d51.5599974!4d-9.1461182\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>! He rules the inside of it, the Otherworldly S\u00edd mound) and is very concerned about the time he loses an eye which would remove him from kingship. However, Dian Cecht heals it, and he retains his authority. Commands his people to reshape Ireland itself as part of his payment to Eochaid to win \u00c9ta\u00edn from him. Further, his names has an entemological link with the Old Irish <i>Midithir</i>, the verb 'to Judge'.</li> <li><b>Prosperity</b>: Midir is stupid rich, even for one of the Tuatha. The third section of <i>Tochmarc \u00c9ta\u00edne</i> is him waving around his massive wealth to intentionally lose gambles with Eochaid until he lures him into a false sense of superiority to keep betting until he can raise the stakes high enough to get \u00c9ta\u00edn.</li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 01-28-2018, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type