racticed polygamy with a 'primary wife' system) F\u00faammnach. Is willing to go to great lengths, pay massive prices, and cause others to commit colossal socitial violations to get his prize.</li> <li><b>Lover</b>: Midir's largest myth, <i>Tochmarc \u00c9ta\u00edne</i> (which you can read <a href=\"http://www.maryjones.us/ctexts/etain.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>!), is the story of his adoration for the woman \u00c9ta\u00edn, chasing her through a thousand years, and different reincarnations, loving her even when she was a giant (albeit very useful) fly. Willing to do horrible things for love.</li> <li><b>Trickster</b>: Midir accomplishes his goals through manipulating, tricking, and decieving others. In his final gambit to win \u00c9ta\u00edn from her most recent husband Eochaid, he not only uses a word ploy to steal \u00c9ta\u00edn from him, but then in an act of furious vengeance, tricks Eochaid into having a child with his own daughter with \u00c9ta\u00edn after tricking him into thinking the daughter was \u00c9ta\u00edn. (This is a <i>very big deal</i> in Ireland, they don't like incest at all)</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Purviews</b><ul><li><b>Deception</b>: Magically tricks Ailill into falling into a Wasting Sickness for \u00c9ta\u00edn so he can disguise himself as him to sleep with her, may have been the source of Aengus Og's trick to take the Brug from Elcmar (probably Nuadu). His final lie to Eochaid is really rather complex, and results in Eochaid committing the large taboo of incest.</li> <li><b>Order</b>: Midir is the R\u00edg (chief / king) of Br\u00ed L\u00e9ith (modernly known as Ardagh Hill, Co. Cork. You can see it <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/maps/place/Ardagh+Hill,+Ardagh,+Unionhall,+Co.+Cork,+Ireland/@51.5598221,-9.1465602,499m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m13!1m7!3m6!1s0x4845ae97fe27e72f:0xa9ae4675984e5e46!2sArdagh+Hill,+Ardagh,+Unionhall,+Co.+Cork,+Ireland!3b1!8m2!3d51.5593202!4d-9.1449504!3m4!1s0x4845ae97fe27e72f:0xa9ae4675984e5e46!8m2!3d51.5599974!4d-9.1461182\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>! He rules the inside of it, the Otherworldly S\u00edd mound) and is very concerned about the time he loses an eye which would remove him from kingship. However, Dian Cecht heals it, and he retains his authority. Commands his people to reshape Ireland itself as part of his payment to Eochaid to win \u00c9ta\u00edn from him. Further, his names has an entemological link with the Old Irish <i>Midithir</i>, the verb 'to Judge'.</li> <li><b>Prosperity</b>: Midir is stupid rich, even for one of the Tuatha. The third section of <i>Tochmarc \u00c9ta\u00edne</i> is him waving around his massive wealth to intentionally lose gambles with Eochaid until he lures him into a false sense of superiority to keep betting until he can raise the stakes high enough to get \u00c9ta\u00edn.</li> </ul></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div> Why were the Irish so concerned with physical perfection? Nuada can't be king without an arm,Midhir can't be chief without an eye,it's kinda unfair. really nice write up by the way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T19:19:36-08:00","id":1180322,"title":"","content":"Just because I like to spread the info here are recordings I made of some of the words in Watcher's post (in Modern Irish):<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/vtoz0pmt2lvpkbbjzsu7egho63pwnl37\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/vtoz0pmt2lvpkbbjzsu7egho63pwnl37\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/vtoz0pmt2lvpkbbjzsu7egho63pwnl37\" target=\"_blank\"> https://app.box.com/s/vtoz0pmt2lvpkbbjzsu7egho63pwnl37 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":". 02-02-2018, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T19:40:35-08:00","id":1180326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180300#post1180300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Midir</b><span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Pronounced: Mithir)</span>*stuff*</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy crap... I was expecting &quot;This is (Random Irish Dude), he totally be a Hunter, with like Epic Dex and stuff...&quot;, but that's a whole and complete write up... Thank you so much!<br /> <br /> As to his unorthodoxy, I don't mind at all, he's so full of flaws, and flavor, that ideas of how to use him in a backstory just leap off the screen. I can just see him now, trying to interact with a descendant who dislikes his &quot;trickster&quot; ways... oh the drama...<br /> <br /> Really, this is perfect... just... wow!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 01-28-2018, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T02:19:50-08:00","id":1180370,"title":"","content":"So.. no character sheet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23785-vonigner","name":"vonigner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T04:34:19-08:00","id":1180382,"title":"","content":"Any idea of what calling and boon Ullr/Uller should have???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T05:29:32-08:00","id":1180392,"title":"","content":"I might be one of the guys who has less trouble with the preview <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> love the starter! Can't wait for the main course!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> very good job!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T06:32:11-08:00","id":1180406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180382#post1180382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any idea of what calling and boon Ullr/Uller should have???</div> </div> </div> </div>For Callings, Hunter is obviously a must. For the other two, I'd say.......Warrior and Guardian? I guess? <br /> <br /> Purviews? Definitely Frost and Wild. Maybe some Epic Dexterity too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T08:47:30-08:00","id":1180428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180326#post1180326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy crap... I was expecting &quot;This is (Random Irish Dude), he totally be a Hunter, with like Epic Dex and stuff...&quot;, but that's a whole and complete write up... Thank you so much!<br /> <br /> As to his unorthodoxy, I don't mind at all, he's so full of flaws, and flavor, that ideas of how to use him in a backstory just leap off the screen. I can just see him now, trying to interact with a descendant who dislikes his &quot;trickster&quot; ways... oh the drama...<br /> <br /> Really, this is perfect... just... wow!</div> </div> </div> </div>I am glad to be of service! I don't do things in half measures, so doing a smaller little write up like that I thought would work best. He is a pretty interesting figure. My Adviser suspects that Midir was actually a rather important figure at one point who we have a very spotty record of. He seems to be important through so many texts, but is inconsistently involved. However, his presence in the Wooing of \u00c9ta\u00edn is a really big marker of him being important in some way. I wish you the best of luck in using him in your games!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180322#post1180322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because I like to spread the info here are recordings I made of some of the words in Watcher's post (in Modern Irish):<br /> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/pquahmt9d11ebg8h8okrllrmswth32zb\" target=\"_blank\">https://app.box.com/s/pquahmt9d11ebg8h8okrllrmswth32zb</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much An Fhuiseog! It is always awesome to have your pronunciations. I was sure I was pronouncing \u00c9ta\u00edn incorrectly in my head, that helped clear it up!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180312#post1180312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why were the Irish so concerned with physical perfection? Nuada can't be king without an arm,Midhir can't be chief without an eye,it's kinda unfair. really nice write up by the way</div> </div> </div> </div>The Irish had a concern with Perfection and Excellence in whatever it was that you did. If you read Irish Sagas, you will notice there are a lot of &quot;most beautiful woman in Ireland,&quot; or &quot;most famed warrior in Ireland,&quot; or &quot;most just king in Ireland&quot; which relates to this. Whatever it is that you did, you should be doing it with overwhelming greatness. Therefore, Kings needed to be 'Unblemished,' their political-religious superiority over others needed to be justified by being 'Unblemished' as rulers. This involved physical blemishes, but mental disabilities, poor judgement, unfair rulings, and poor hospitality count as 'Blemishes' against their kingship. Both Nuadu's loss of his arm/hand (the word in Old Irish can mean either) and Bres' bad hospitality count as 'Blemishes' against their kingship.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Warriors could be riddled in scars, scars, especially fresh red scars, are regarded as being a mark of honor as we can see in an argument between Conall Cernach and his father at the end of The Destruction of Da Derga's Hostel, where his father reprimands him for failing to save Conare, and Conall simply responds by telling his father that his wounds were red and fresh, while his father's scars were faded white. These fresh scars were marks of their excellence as warriors, and were therefore good things to have.<br /> <br /> It all comes down to being the Best and Greatest. Not being 'Excellent' like the Greeks with the notion of Arete, but overwhelming utter domination, and skill to the point of blatant supernatural levels of function, such as the various Heroic Feats of C\u00faChulainn, such as The Thunder Feat or The Heroic Salmon Leap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T17:07:47-08:00","id":1180546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180406#post1180406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For Callings, Hunter is obviously a must. For the other two, I'd say.......Warrior and Guardian? I guess?<br /> <br /> Purviews? Definitely Frost and Wild. Maybe some Epic Dexterity too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd swap out Guardian for Liminal and add Journeys. His only surviving myths involve him traversing the seas on a magic bone, and his association with skiing also ties into being connected with Travel. Maybe even Order? Depends on exactly what order encompasses. Oaths were sworn on him and he lead the Aesir for a hot second. I could see Judge or Leader, but Warrior, Hunter and Liminal seem like the best callings to go with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13472-~nkf~","name":"~NKF~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T18:54:42-08:00","id":1180565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180428#post1180428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you so much An Fhuiseog! It is always awesome to have your pronunciations. I was sure I was pronouncing \u00c9ta\u00edn incorrectly in my head, that helped clear it up!</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably are correct for old Irish, like Midir was &quot;Mithir&quot; in Old but is now &quot;Meej&quot; in Modern. I've added a few more from the Origins:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/vtoz0pmt2lvpkbbjzsu7egho63pwnl37\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/vtoz0pmt2lvpkbbjzsu7egho63pwnl37\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/vtoz0pmt2lvpkbbjzsu7egho63pwnl37\" target=\"_blank\"> https://app.box.com/s/vtoz0pmt2lvpkbbjzsu7egho63pwnl37 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T19:06:56-08:00","id":1180571,"title":"","content":"I'm a little bummed how few of the Supernatural Paths fit the non-European Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T19:34:04-08:00","id":1180578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180571#post1180571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little bummed how few of the Supernatural Paths fit the non-European Pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>By Supernatural paths you mean... the 2 skills associated with each pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T20:03:59-08:00","id":1180581,"title":"","content":"Query: Are we good to share the document, with our gaming group, say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T20:05:49-08:00","id":1180582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180578#post1180578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By Supernatural paths you mean... the 2 skills associated with each pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>No those are the path skills, I think Jakki meant the Kitsune-Satyr-Wolf Warrior-Therianthrope ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T20:18:13-08:00","id":1180588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180582#post1180582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No those are the path skills, I think Jakki meant the Kitsune-Satyr-Wolf Warrior-Therianthrope ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I was surprised we got any in Origins. I thought we would have to wait until the Companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T20:19:26-08:00","id":1180589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180588#post1180588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. I was surprised we got any in Origins. I thought we would have to wait until the Companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wish we'd gotten any that fit the Netjer, Teotl, Devas, or Manitou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T20:24:06-08:00","id":1180590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180589#post1180589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just wish we'd gotten any that fit the Netjer, Teotl, Devas, or Manitou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure Therianthrope can work for the Teotl just fine. Jaguar shifters and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T22:14:55-08:00","id":1180610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180589#post1180589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just wish we'd gotten any that fit the Netjer, Teotl, Devas, or Manitou.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Alpharius said, Therianthropes and Wolf-Warriors* are neigh universal, and aren't the Deer Woman supposed to be from Manitou myths?<br /> <br /> *Wolf-Warriors even calls out to the Rathi from Hindu mythology by name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 01-30-2018, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T22:21:38-08:00","id":1180611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180589#post1180589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just wish we'd gotten any that fit the Netjer, Teotl, Devas, or Manitou.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, wolf-warrior is mentioned to work for any example of &quot;badass warrior who fights for an ideal&quot; and that depending on the exact knacks you take and how you fluff stuff can be used for pretty much any pantheon. I think wolf-warrior was just used as a place holder name, and the text specifically calls out that the path can be used to make an amazon, a berserker, or a rathi. <br /> <br /> Similarly, they present the Deer Lady as a variant satyr as an example of how you can modify the existing paths to cover cultural concepts different from the original. <br /> <br /> I mean, we certainly got few enough that it feels like the ones we got were mostly meant to be the most obvious/popular ones that were meant to give us a starting point to play with and potentially make our own. I personally feel like they probably could have fit another one or two in from some more diverse pantheons, but it is what it is and between Hero, the Companion and I think maybe the Bestiary we're getting more so there's that to look forward to.<br /> <br /> Although, according to the text, there were supposed to be seven modified paths total: three wolf-warrior variants, three satyr, and one that was just an animal. However,while we got the three promised wolf-warrior variants, we only got two satyr variants and no modified path that was an animal, unless the Cu Sith was supposed to be down in that section instead of right above it. Any explanation for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T11:38:46-08:00","id":1180822,"title":"","content":"I skimmed most of this pdf...I was a little thrown when &quot;Wesir&quot; was mentioned under Osiris in the appendix...(I did know, and I'm sure most of us will know Osiris' alternate name)<br /> <br /> For the most part, I enjoyed reading it. It was well-written to me. Sure some things probably needed some polish (I'm still reading it), and I'm sure some may have issues with the game mechanics, but overall I'm looking forward to the end-product. It looks to be an auspicious beginning for Scion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T11:46:45-08:00","id":1180827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180611#post1180611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, according to the text, there were supposed to be seven modified paths total: three wolf-warrior variants, three satyr, and one that was just an animal. However,while we got the three promised wolf-warrior variants, we only got two satyr variants and no modified path that was an animal, unless the Cu Sith was supposed to be down in that section instead of right above it. Any explanation for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, I think the Kitsune was meant to be an example of a supernatural animal (i.e., a fox that turns into a person) and the C\u00fa Sith is a variant on that (a dog that definitely doesn't turn into a person). At least, that was my idea when I wrote it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T15:29:22-08:00","id":1180899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoffrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180827#post1180827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, I think the Kitsune was meant to be an example of a supernatural animal (i.e., a fox that turns into a person) and the C\u00fa Sith is a variant on that (a dog that definitely doesn't turn into a person). At least, that was my idea when I wrote it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate on your decision to give them Imperfect Disguise as a knack? What benefit do you see them getting out of it? Is it supposed to have...any upside at all? If not, why would anyone take it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T15:50:50-08:00","id":1180911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorsRattus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180899#post1180899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you elaborate on your decision to give them Imperfect Disguise as a knack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. You and I might be looking at different versions of the text. The one that I have doesn't have it as a knack (for just the reasons that you point out: no one would take it voluntarily). It was in there in an earlier version, though marked as a drawback (something you acquired by virtue of who you are, like European werewolves being vulnerable to silver) rather than a knack you chose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T15:55:44-08:00","id":1180915,"title":"","content":"Imperfect Disguise appears in the list of so-called Sandbags: traits that are explicitly disadvantages. It's not something that you willingly take; it's a characteristic that you *must* take if you're going to play that kind of character.<br /> <br /> Kitsune, for example, are famous for having their identities given away when someone somehow spots their tail(s). It just wouldn't be true to Kitsune myths if they didn't have that kind of disadvantage. The same for many other types of non-human: in stories, their true nature is always found out because they can't quite pass for human. They don't have a shadow, or they turn into beasts at the full moon.<br /> <br /> So you're right, it's not convenient to have Imperfect Disguise, but it's definitely in keeping with the myths about certain creatures. It's the sort of thing a Story Guide would probably insist on.<br /> <br /> ---Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T16:20:49-08:00","id":1180927,"title":"","content":"It is definitely listed as a knack in the templates in the appendix of the pdf that went out to backers. I am totally fine with it being an innate trait of the templates - but that isn\u2019t what we have at present. Eating a knack slot for the ability to play a kitsune is awful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T18:08:32-08:00","id":1180952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180382#post1180382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any idea of what calling and boon Ullr/Uller should have???</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ullr</b>, God of Winter, Archery and the Hunt</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Callings: Hunter, Judge, Warrior<br /> Purviews: Epic Dexterity, Journeys, Frost, Order, Artistry (Bows), Water*<br /> <br /> <br /> *Note, Water is arguable for Ullr as we have evidence of stories in connection to him having a great ship and prominent kennings relating to it, but the myth doesin't actually survive in any form and is therefore semi-appropriate to leave out. </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T22:16:04-08:00","id":1181016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorsRattus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180927#post1180927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is definitely listed as a knack in the templates in the appendix of the pdf that went out to backers. I am totally fine with it being an innate trait of the templates - but that isn\u2019t what we have at present. Eating a knack slot for the ability to play a kitsune is awful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a page reference, because I'm looking at my copy of the backer pdf and I can't find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1529-srgrvsalot","name":"SrGrvsaLot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T23:04:22-08:00","id":1181026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SrGrvsaLot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1181016#post1181016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have a page reference, because I'm looking at my copy of the backer pdf and I can't find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, not seeing it here either. NPC kitsune got Imperfect Disguise as a negative quality (<span style=\"font-size:8px\">which this, out of all the games in the world, is probably the only one to call it a sandbag instead of a flaw or something like that XD</span>), while the kitsune path for PCs has the tail as a persistent Condition that gives you momentum when it troubles you, and no Imperfect Disguise in the knack list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T00:05:31-08:00","id":1181033,"title":"","content":"Kitsune was a bad example. It\u2019s on the Cu Sith list (199) and Deer Woman (201).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T01:04:46-08:00","id":1181041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorsRattus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1181033#post1181033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kitsune was a bad example. It\u2019s on the Cu Sith list (199) and Deer Woman (201).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's strictly optional for the Cu Sith, isn't it? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Breed Versatility: C\u00fa Sith can choose any one of the following Knacks to represent their specific breed: any one Hunter Knack or Imperfect Disguise (white fur and red eyes, Antagonist Quality). </div> </div> </div>Just take a Hunter knack and you don't have any problems with your disguise.<br /> <br /> As for the Deer Woman, I can't work out what's going on there - Is that a list of Knacks all Deer Women have active all the time? Is that a list of Knacks they possess, but can only have the normal amount (1 at Origin) active? Or is that a list of additional knacks they can choose from?<br /> <br /> I think I'm going to have to read the supernatural paths stuff through again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T03:24:11-08:00","id":1181063,"title":"","content":"I have a total different question concerning Initiative.<br /> <br /> 1) I have read that characters' turn are different by using the initiative pool every Round, but now, if, say, X is in the first slot, X remains in the first slot as long as the Initiative Roster is needed, am I correct? <br /> <br /> 2) No one acts in the same slot anymore? In the 1st edition, many characters could act in, say, tick 5. Is it removed or just not detailed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T06:03:40-08:00","id":1181107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180294#post1180294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not familiar with Aberrant, so I can't comment on similarities. But with NPCs and PCs using different rules for defending (PC defense is rolled, while NPC defense is a static difficulty that the attacker needs to overcome), NPCs don't have an option to use full defense - instead, the size of their defense values look like it's assumed that they're automatically full defending, but can still act. They also don't take injury conditions. So, basically, unless they get taken out entirely or are hit by something that causes a condition other than damage, they both attack and defend at full capacity.<br /> <br /> It might actually be to many characters' benefit to go last, so they know if they need to full defend or not in any given round.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also normal defend doesn't have to just raise difficulty, the dive for cover stunt would straight up block damage. And the roll away stunt would be good for avoiding melee or thrown attacks at the very least. I think that gives sufficient options that unless your party gets caught totally unprepared in a bad position they can probably keep themselves alive. Combine that with some disabling stunts in the initial rounds and damage isn't a massive issue.<br /> <br /> Besides, what good adventure doesn't end with the battered heroes facing down the smug, immaculate bad guy after overcoming all his minions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T21:51:24-08:00","id":1181330,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a> How are natural unnamed attacks supposed to be handled? The lycans can use momentum to add lethal and the deer women can stomp on people with their hooves but it never mentions what tags a base unarmed attack should have compared to say knuckle dusters.<br /> <br /> Are we supposed to just treat them as worn weapons and give them whatever tags we deem appropriate?<br /> <br /> Also, if that's the case then would knuckle dusters weapons be counted as unarmed in regards to unarmed knacks? <br /> <br /> Just want to know your take on it because I know a player of mine will want to make a brawler. I figure most of this likely comes down to ST choice due to the amount of possible natural attacks there could be but figured I'd ask and see if it spawns a couple sentences covering it under weapons or something. <br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T11:42:09-08:00","id":1181452,"title":"","content":"Did anyone else realize Emanuel Montero name means &quot;God With Us?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T19:23:44-08:00","id":1181550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1181452#post1181452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did anyone else realize Emanuel Montero name means &quot;God With Us?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate is very unsubtle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T08:58:45-08:00","id":1181675,"title":"","content":"I'm still not happy with the execution of Specialties, since they don't really help you succeed on the applicable rolls.<br /> <br /> I mean, they COULD if you turn around and use the Momentum on them. But since <br /> <br /> a.) Momentum is a shared pool among players, and <br /> <br /> b.) Momentum is skill-agnostic<br /> <br /> You declaring that your character has a specialty in seduction doesn't necessarily mean that you're any better than someone who doesn't. Someone's going to have a good time with the bonus momentum from your failure, but it isn't necessarily going to be you. Your repeated failures at flirting could eventually turn out in your favor...or it could translate to a devastating left hook for your buddy when a bar fight breaks out.<br /> <br /> And maybe it sounds a littler selfish to be phrasing it like that. And maybe it's a little old-fashioned of me focusing on how it's been handled in previous iterations, but it really, <i>really</i> bothers me that this is how Storypath handles specialties. Traditionally it's been saying &quot;This is a focus of mine. This is what I'm good at.&quot; Here? Not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T12:03:15-08:00","id":1181745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1181675#post1181675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And maybe it sounds a littler selfish to be phrasing it like that. And maybe it's a little old-fashioned of me focusing on how it's been handled in previous iterations, but it really, <i>really</i> bothers me that this is how Storypath handles specialties. Traditionally it's been saying &quot;This is a focus of mine. This is what I'm good at.&quot; Here? Not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there IS a circumstance where it gives you a bonus. When the topic comes up in another skill.<br /> <br /> The example given on page 105:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For every Skill that ends up with three or more dots, choose a Specialty (p. XX). Specialties are only free during character creation. A Specialty is narrowly focused expertise within a Skill. For example, Firearms grants skill with all ranged weapons that use gunpowder, but a character may have a Specialty in Pistols. Once a character has a Specialty, she may apply that expertise as a 1-point Enhancement to other, related Skills, such as convincing a group of soldiers to buy pistols from Fenris Arms. Additionally, if she fails a roll in an Ability in which she has a Specialty (such as missing a character with a Firearms action) she gains an additional point of Momentum. </div> </div> </div>An example I can think of that is like... Having a Survival Specialty in &quot;Identifying Herbs&quot; coming up in a Medicine roll because &quot;Oh, we're in a forest, oh hey, this is an herb that can sterilize wounds&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T13:04:18-08:00","id":1181767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1181745#post1181745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there IS a circumstance where it gives you a bonus. When the topic comes up in another skill.<br /> <br /> The example given on page 105:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> An example I can think of that is like... Having a Survival Specialty in &quot;Identifying Herbs&quot; coming up in a Medicine roll because &quot;Oh, we're in a forest, oh hey, this is an herb that can sterilize wounds&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Or with the seduction specialty mentioned, assuming it's for persuasion, a bonus on subterfuge because you're flirting, or Leadership because they want to impress you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T13:18:13-08:00","id":1181776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1181745#post1181745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there IS a circumstance where it gives you a bonus. When the topic comes up in another skill.<br /> <br /> An example I can think of that is like... Having a Survival Specialty in &quot;Identifying Herbs&quot; coming up in a Medicine roll because &quot;Oh, we're in a forest, oh hey, this is an herb that can sterilize wounds&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, complaint not entirely withdrawn, but...notably mitigated, I suppose?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T13:24:57-08:00","id":1181778,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the 1e bonus to other Skills is a really nice bonus to me. I like it because it encourages using more varied dice-pools, and synergy between Skills. I don't have to worry about making sure I have a relevant specialty in every Skill so my sword making character knows basic metallurgy, and the history of blades, and how much to price a sword. I know that having that specialty gets me that enhancement even if I'm not rolling the Skill I got it from. <br /> <br /> I mean, what are the odds of a character that wants to be a master pistol duelist already having such good stats that another 1e from a specialty for shooting people is going to be that big of a difference? Or +1 die? Or whatever small bonus you'd get?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T13:34:12-08:00","id":1181780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1181776#post1181776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, complaint not entirely withdrawn, but...notably mitigated, I suppose?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do get what you mean. I found it different as well, but I'm willing to give it a try to see how it feels before making any real conclusions about it.<br /> <br /> I totally get a reaction of &quot;... Well, that's different.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T13:57:03-08:00","id":1181785,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was definitely in the same initial boat about Specialties, but after thinking about it, I actually really like the way Scion does it and honestly, I'll probably be stealing it for other games/systems, stitching it onto whatever existing Specialty system the game in question has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T14:02:29-08:00","id":1181788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1181778#post1181778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the 1e bonus to other Skills is a really nice bonus to me. I like it because it encourages using more varied dice-pools, and synergy between Skills. I don't have to worry about making sure I have a relevant specialty in every Skill so my sword making character knows basic metallurgy, and the history of blades, and how much to price a sword. I know that having that specialty gets me that enhancement even if I'm not rolling the Skill I got it from. <br /> <br /> I mean, what are the odds of a character that wants to be a master pistol duelist already having such good stats that another 1e from a specialty for shooting people is going to be that big of a difference? Or +1 die? Or whatever small bonus you'd get?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, kudos to you for making a connection that I somehow missed. A Close Combat specialty in Swords, and you get 1E on the Culture check to go &quot;Guys, this is no ordinary sword. That's the Honjo Masamune&quot; and realize that the Kami would be forever grateful if you return it to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T14:41:04-08:00","id":1181808,"title":"","content":"Can't take too much credit there. The popularity of the Interdisciplinary Specialty Merit from the CofD games in my group has this as an essentially standard component of a lot of characters (why pay for a dozen specialties when you can buy a Merit the same price as one, and have an existing Specialty apply to every Skill?). Storypath just goes ahead and makes it the default bonus instead of one you buy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T16:01:35-08:00","id":1181835,"title":"","content":"Also in terms of the momentum bonus, this is a world where fate is alive, more powerful than the gods, and operates on the rule of drama. A swordsman missing every attack against a tough foe before landing a solid one is dramatic, but just as dramatic is the swordsman being held off until the scholar that can barely shoot straight lands a lucky shot through his eye, or the target is escaping and you having plenty of bonus dice for the high speed chase.<br /> <br /> A lot of stuff in this system makes more sense if you remember the universe literally runs on dramatic tropes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T17:12:23-08:00","id":1181857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1181835#post1181835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also in terms of the momentum bonus, this is a world where fate is alive, more powerful than the gods, and operates on the rule of drama. A swordsman missing every attack against a tough foe before landing a solid one is dramatic, but just as dramatic is the swordsman being held off until the scholar that can barely shoot straight lands a lucky shot through his eye, or the target is escaping and you having plenty of bonus dice for the high speed chase.<br /> <br /> A lot of stuff in this system makes more sense if you remember the universe literally runs on dramatic tropes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of Rocky IV when Rocky, against all odds, cuts Drago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T21:54:26-08:00","id":118