ll the 1st Edition pdfs, and not the 2nd editions ones, so you wouldn\u2019t be getting the preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T22:52:28-08:00","id":1182819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1182818#post1182818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *checks the kickstarter*<br /> <br /> Ah, there\u2019s the problem. The \u201cKnowledgable Mortal\u201d tier you pledged is for the reward of all the 1st Edition pdfs, and not the 2nd editions ones, so you wouldn\u2019t be getting the preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see...well I guess i know what I'm upgrading in the next week or so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1268-cosmic-mind","name":"Cosmic Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1268_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T02:53:36-08:00","id":1182849,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar561_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"561\" data-vbnamecard=\"561\">Mockery</a> if you have any issue with the blackpool as a common pool, Neal wrote in the preview that players can have their own blackpools. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T22:18:26-08:00","id":1183165,"title":"","content":"How do we get to this Backerkit? I got my PDF through my email updates but I never heard anything about a Backerkit.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure if it's just because I've gotten so used to reading PDF's of RPG's in a certain way or not but this feels like it's just missing something. I don't know what that something is but I do know that it feels like it's missing SOMETHING and it's one of those things that as soon as someone points it out to me I'll be like &quot;Yup, that was it&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T22:59:31-08:00","id":1183174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1183165#post1183165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do we get to this Backerkit? I got my PDF through my email updates but I never heard anything about a Backerkit.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure if it's just because I've gotten so used to reading PDF's of RPG's in a certain way or not but this feels like it's just missing something. I don't know what that something is but I do know that it feels like it's missing SOMETHING and it's one of those things that as soon as someone points it out to me I'll be like &amp;quot;Yup, that was it&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Bookmarks. :V","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T10:31:08-08:00","id":1183298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1183174#post1183174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bookmarks. :V</div> </div> </div> </div>I painstakingly went through my draft and put in bookmarks.<br /> <br /> I mean it took like two days of multitask working so it's not like it took me a lot of time but-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T11:52:49-08:00","id":1183337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1183165#post1183165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do we get to this Backerkit? I got my PDF through my email updates but I never heard anything about a Backerkit.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure if it's just because I've gotten so used to reading PDF's of RPG's in a certain way or not but this feels like it's just missing something. I don't know what that something is but I do know that it feels like it's missing SOMETHING and it's one of those things that as soon as someone points it out to me I'll be like &quot;Yup, that was it&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My email was from backerkit rather than Kickstarter. Maybe that's what's confusing you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T09:06:18-08:00","id":1183614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1183337#post1183337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My email was from backerkit rather than Kickstarter. Maybe that's what's confusing you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh okay, I was thinking this was something else. I didn't realize it was another thing like Kickstarter. That makes more sense now \ud83e\udd23","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T09:42:30-08:00","id":1183620,"title":"","content":"Backerkit is a website used to magage Kickstarter rewards. You should have received an email to fill out your backer survey if you backed the Kickstarter which set up your Backerkit account.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T08:22:25-08:00","id":1183944,"title":"","content":"I have read through it twice now. I understand people are focused on the character creation rules and the crunch. I am pleased with how folks are resolving them and running through options.<br /> <br /> I have a criticism for the book; it feels incomplete. I do not mean 'oh we need the divine rules'. The setting feels lacking.<br /> <br /> For example, is there a Catholic church? Do the Abrahamic faiths exist at all? There is the saint path, cool. But it lacks context. Indeed, that is the entire issue with the book; the crunch is absolutely brilliant, new, and different. There is this great potential in it, but it 'feels' like it exists in a vacuum.<br /> <br /> I have no problem homebrewing a little setting, but my storyteller was immediately turned off, turned up her nose and declared she didn't have the time (which is fair) or inclination (also fair) to do so. I went back to reread it, and really... it is lacking in setting. It needs more context.<br /> <br /> I am hoping that will be found in Hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1199-mister-lion","name":"Mister Lion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T09:12:28-08:00","id":1183960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister Lion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1183944#post1183944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have read through it twice now. I understand people are focused on the character creation rules and the crunch. I am pleased with how folks are resolving them and running through options.<br /> <br /> I have a criticism for the book; it feels incomplete. I do not mean 'oh we need the divine rules'. The setting feels lacking.<br /> <br /> For example, is there a Catholic church? Do the Abrahamic faiths exist at all? There is the saint path, cool. But it lacks context. Indeed, that is the entire issue with the book; the crunch is absolutely brilliant, new, and different. There is this great potential in it, but it 'feels' like it exists in a vacuum.<br /> <br /> I have no problem homebrewing a little setting, but my storyteller was immediately turned off, turned up her nose and declared she didn't have the time (which is fair) or inclination (also fair) to do so. I went back to reread it, and really... it is lacking in setting. It needs more context.<br /> <br /> I am hoping that will be found in Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe book specifically states that the Abrahamic faiths are still around and that they're still the dominant religions in the World. They just don't have the near-total control that they have in our World because the Pagan traditions never died out as thoroughly as they did in our World. <br /> <br /> \u200bThe context of the Saint Path is that you're a person whose soul resonates strongly with one of the Pantheon's Virtues. To the point where you can actually do great things on your own, provided you stay true to those Virtues. <br /> <br /> \u200bThe books also mention that the nations of the World have different ways of dealing with the pockets of mythic creatures that still exist in the World. They have esoteric and rarely-used laws for dealing with said creatures and that magic itself is pretty much an illegal activity in most areas. <br /> <br /> \u200bYeah, I'd like a full setting book that really dives into more examples, too. But there's definitely enough material to at least get an idea of what the World of Scion is like: it's our World, just with surviving pockets of ancient religions and mythic creatures hidden within it. You can justify saying that the US Government may have a division of the FBI that deals with lycanthropy cases, or investigations into possible Sorcerous activities. You can justify saying that the Irish are probably even MORE superstitious about the woods and faerie hills in their country than they are in the real World. Heck, even in our World, the Irish still don't pave over faerie circles. Imagine how much more they'd be if the fae were very, very real, and still had power and influence within Ireland? You could say that the UK has a special service secreted away, ready to come rushing in if King Arthur ever returns from Avalon when England's need is greatest. <br /> <br /> \u200bTons of options with what's been shown already. You just need to use some imagination. And as the line goes on, we'll almost certainly get more dedicated setting books from which to draw further inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T10:02:15-08:00","id":1183984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1183960#post1183960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThe book specifically states that the Abrahamic faiths are still around and that they're still the dominant religions in the World. They just don't have the near-total control that they have in our World because the Pagan traditions never died out as thoroughly as they did in our World.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe context of the Saint Path is that you're a person whose soul resonates strongly with one of the Pantheon's Virtues. To the point where you can actually do great things on your own, provided you stay true to those Virtues.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe books also mention that the nations of the World have different ways of dealing with the pockets of mythic creatures that still exist in the World. They have esoteric and rarely-used laws for dealing with said creatures and that magic itself is pretty much an illegal activity in most areas.<br /> <br /> \u200bYeah, I'd like a full setting book that really dives into more examples, too. But there's definitely enough material to at least get an idea of what the World of Scion is like: it's our World, just with surviving pockets of ancient religions and mythic creatures hidden within it. You can justify saying that the US Government may have a division of the FBI that deals with lycanthropy cases, or investigations into possible Sorcerous activities. You can justify saying that the Irish are probably even MORE superstitious about the woods and faerie hills in their country than they are in the real World. Heck, even in our World, the Irish still don't pave over faerie circles. Imagine how much more they'd be if the fae were very, very real, and still had power and influence within Ireland? You could say that the UK has a special service secreted away, ready to come rushing in if King Arthur ever returns from Avalon when England's need is greatest.<br /> <br /> \u200bTons of options with what's been shown already. You just need to use some imagination. And as the line goes on, we'll almost certainly get more dedicated setting books from which to draw further inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tons? No sir. I walked away from two reads with very little grasp on the setting. This is an origin book. You and I? I assume we both played the game, and we are really comfortable making our own assumptions and decisions about how the world works.<br /> <br /> The 19 year old picking this out on Drivethru? She might not be. This is the first book needed of 4. Another chapter giving a more detailed sketch of the setting would go a long way here.<br /> <br /> Let me say again, this is meant as constructive criticism. I'm not meaning to troll or be a wet blanket. I'm still excited about the book and the game. I do not regret kickstarting the product. I think that an origin's book should nail down the setting a bit more than this does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1199-mister-lion","name":"Mister Lion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T11:17:23-08:00","id":1184017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister Lion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1183984#post1183984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Tons? No sir. I walked away from two reads with very little grasp on the setting. This is an origin book. You and I? I assume we both played the game, and we are really comfortable making our own assumptions and decisions about how the world works.<br /> <br /> The 19 year old picking this out on Drivethru? She might not be. This is the first book needed of 4. Another chapter giving a more detailed sketch of the setting would go a long way here.<br /> <br /> Let me say again, this is meant as constructive criticism. I'm not meaning to troll or be a wet blanket. I'm still excited about the book and the game. I do not regret kickstarting the product. I think that an origin's book should nail down the setting a bit more than this does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found the setting to be fairly fleshed out in how the supernatural interacts with the mundane. I'd say most of the more vague pieces are there to allow more wiggle room for gms to decide what myths are most prevalent in which areas, and what exactly the local supernatural comuniteis are like. The gm section also talks abound keeping most of the supernatural stuff behind the curtain for now, something in the corner of your eye, a gut feeling. So really, knowing that Abrahamic religions still had almost as much influence as they did on our Earth and the governements have a few semi-classified ways to deal with it while normal folks still throw salt over their shoulders is probably enough until they start to interact with the mythic more casually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T13:19:31-08:00","id":1184057,"title":"","content":"I feel like the setting is pretty well communicated - especially in co trust with 1E, where there was no setting at all on the mortal level.<br /> <br /> That said, an extra chapter\u2019s length on Origins-level antagonists would be helpful in communicating what PCs can occupy their time with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T14:44:44-08:00","id":1184091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184017#post1184017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I found the setting to be fairly fleshed out in how the supernatural interacts with the mundane. I'd say most of the more vague pieces are there to allow more wiggle room for gms to decide what myths are most prevalent in which areas, and what exactly the local supernatural comuniteis are like. The gm section also talks abound keeping most of the supernatural stuff behind the curtain for now, something in the corner of your eye, a gut feeling. So really, knowing that Abrahamic religions still had almost as much influence as they did on our Earth and the governements have a few semi-classified ways to deal with it while normal folks still throw salt over their shoulders is probably enough until they start to interact with the mythic more casually.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that is the way it works, with more of the weirdness being in the hero book, okay. I worry I am not communicating properly. Please forgive me if I am doing so, or if I am repeating myself out of the fear of doing so. Text can be imprecise.<br /> <br /> I will speak in generalities. I still don't know if the typical American family goes to the temple of the Tuatha, or a grove for the kami, or to temple, or church on Sunday, these are the things that I am talking about. How the world looks different. Not about Men in Black stealing Scions and dissecting them. I mean, how the world is different in the mundane. The little quirky details that can catch a player's attention and get them invested in the concept.<br /> <br /> Again, I found the book well organized, smooth, and the crunch looks tighter-- though we haven't had the Hero level stuff yet. I am not trying to pee in cheerios or ruin anyone's fun. It's really cool what I have seen so far. I just think they might sell more books, and while it is fine if us older folks understand it (Been gaming since i was 11, I'm in my 40s now), but I think they would sell more books if they put a little more info out on the setting in the first 50 pages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1199-mister-lion","name":"Mister Lion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T15:07:02-08:00","id":1184098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister Lion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184091#post1184091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that is the way it works, with more of the weirdness being in the hero book, okay. I worry I am not communicating properly. Please forgive me if I am doing so, or if I am repeating myself out of the fear of doing so. Text can be imprecise.<br /> <br /> I will speak in generalities. I still don't know if the typical American family goes to the temple of the Tuatha, or a grove for the kami, or to temple, or church on Sunday, these are the things that I am talking about. How the world looks different. Not about Men in Black stealing Scions and dissecting them. I mean, how the world is different in the mundane. The little quirky details that can catch a player's attention and get them invested in the concept.<br /> <br /> Again, I found the book well organized, smooth, and the crunch looks tighter-- though we haven't had the Hero level stuff yet. I am not trying to pee in cheerios or ruin anyone's fun. It's really cool what I have seen so far. I just think they might sell more books, and while it is fine if us older folks understand it (Been gaming since i was 11, I'm in my 40s now), but I think they would sell more books if they put a little more info out on the setting in the first 50 pages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book does note that Families go to church right next to a temple of the Aesir, which is smaller because of much smaller congregation. But in general most &quot;pagan&quot; worship is private among families, prayer groups, or even just social gatherings where they say what sounds like a silly prayer to a deity. Understandable if you missed it, I think it was buried in with a bunch of other stuff and the lack of layout does blur some stuff. It seems like people that follow the old gods are thought of by the population at larger the way people see any non-mainstream religious movement, a little odd and quirky, but as long as the guys worshiping the teotl don't start drowning kids for teloc it's live and let live unless your a fundementalist wacko.<br /> <br /> Or I hallucinated that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T15:33:01-08:00","id":1184112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister Lion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184091#post1184091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that is the way it works, with more of the weirdness being in the hero book, okay. I worry I am not communicating properly. Please forgive me if I am doing so, or if I am repeating myself out of the fear of doing so. Text can be imprecise.<br /> <br /> I will speak in generalities. I still don't know if the typical American family goes to the temple of the Tuatha, or a grove for the kami, or to temple, or church on Sunday, these are the things that I am talking about. How the world looks different. Not about Men in Black stealing Scions and dissecting them. I mean, how the world is different in the mundane. The little quirky details that can catch a player's attention and get them invested in the concept.<br /> <br /> Again, I found the book well organized, smooth, and the crunch looks tighter-- though we haven't had the Hero level stuff yet. I am not trying to pee in cheerios or ruin anyone's fun. It's really cool what I have seen so far. I just think they might sell more books, and while it is fine if us older folks understand it (Been gaming since i was 11, I'm in my 40s now), but I think they would sell more books if they put a little more info out on the setting in the first 50 pages.</div> </div> </div> </div>More people in the West follow the same major monotheistic (or at least in he Word, intensely Henotheistic) faiths. Active organized polytheistic worship are minority faiths, but unlike in our world, the European, Egyptian, and Aztec varieties have existed continuously rather than being reconstructed.<br /> <br /> Many people who make small sacrifices to Aesir or Teotl when called for may also go to Church on Sundays and don\u2019t feel there\u2019s much of a contradiction there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T16:16:23-08:00","id":1184126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister Lion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184091#post1184091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that is the way it works, with more of the weirdness being in the hero book, okay. I worry I am not communicating properly. Please forgive me if I am doing so, or if I am repeating myself out of the fear of doing so. Text can be imprecise.<br /> <br /> I will speak in generalities. I still don't know if the typical American family goes to the temple of the Tuatha, or a grove for the kami, or to temple, or church on Sunday, these are the things that I am talking about. How the world looks different. Not about Men in Black stealing Scions and dissecting them. I mean, how the world is different in the mundane. The little quirky details that can catch a player's attention and get them invested in the concept.<br /> <br /> Again, I found the book well organized, smooth, and the crunch looks tighter-- though we haven't had the Hero level stuff yet. I am not trying to pee in cheerios or ruin anyone's fun. It's really cool what I have seen so far. I just think they might sell more books, and while it is fine if us older folks understand it (Been gaming since i was 11, I'm in my 40s now), but I think they would sell more books if they put a little more info out on the setting in the first 50 pages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed in a lot of the Pantheon previews from the Kickstarters, they included sections about the religion pertaining to the Pantheon. Maybe in the Heroes book it'll have more of those &quot;And these are the festivals of the Aesir-&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T09:45:53-08:00","id":1184435,"title":"","content":"The lack of in text descriptions of the attributes is driving one of my players up the wall, and I sort of agree with them. I usually happen to have about three CofD books open at the same time I run Scion just because they're leftovers from my playing in another game earlier in the week, so in theory if I wanted to go read a description of just what in the World...Cunning is, I really can just tab over in my pdf reader and read the Wits description in a different book. That should not be the standard for an RPG that stands on its own, and Origins is the core rules of Storypath for the whole Scion line. We, as a relatively long experienced group, don't need those descriptions but the lack of them seems like they'd be really shitty for someone who is just picking this book up as the first OPP product they've ever read. Or first RPG for that matter<br /> <br /> Each skill got a nice long descriptor and list of what 1, 3, and 5 dots means in the grand scheme of 'how good is this <i>really</i>?' but unless I'm missing a page of text somewhere, they aren't in Origins for the attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T13:17:46-08:00","id":1184499,"title":"","content":"Thats actually a really great point and a massive oversight or ommision. We 100% need a attribute description section in the origins book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T16:38:05-08:00","id":1184548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184499#post1184499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats actually a really great point and a massive oversight or ommision. We 100% need a attribute description section in the origins book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll third this motion. That IS a pretty big oversight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T16:47:43-08:00","id":1184554,"title":"","content":"I can't really understand the difference between Primordial and titans and also why not every Pantheon Preview has a Primordial :/ ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T16:56:26-08:00","id":1184557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184554#post1184554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really understand the difference between Primordial and titans and also why not every Pantheon Preview has a Primordial :/ ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the pantheon previews were from earlier drafts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T17:16:58-08:00","id":1184562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184554#post1184554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really understand the difference between Primordial and titans and also why not every Pantheon Preview has a Primordial :/ ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Primordials are vast cosmic beings and do not manifest in the World.<br /> <br /> Titans are their shadow cast on the World instead. They are more dominated by a single Purview than Gods (who are closer tied to humanity), but also narrower in nature than full Primordials. This makes them potentially very dangerous as they carry out their specific aspect of their Purviews' affect on the world.<br /> <br /> Let me put in this way...<br /> <br /> A God of fire is just a divine being who has dominion over fire, but has relatively human judgment (on a much longer time scale) and upholds their Pantheon's Virtues.<br /> <br /> A Primordial of fire encompasses all the positive and negative aspect of fire in balance<br /> <br /> A Titan of fire, unlike a Primordial, can manifest in the World and encompasses only a specific aspect of fire, like it's destructive consumption (Surtr), with no balance from its other aspects. Another Titan of fire may be driven to nurture life and preserve it from entropy without any temperance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T18:31:14-08:00","id":1184585,"title":"","content":"As an aside, I'm so happy I finally get that - when we first started getting teasers I was confused as to how Primordials were vaster and further removed from the world than Titans, but at the same time seemed more humane and less alien. I now get that it's just that they're in-balance while Titans are &quot;smaller&quot; in that they represent specific extremities of the concept the Primordial encompasses all of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T21:13:59-08:00","id":1184609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184554#post1184554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really understand the difference between Primordial and titans and also why not every Pantheon Preview has a Primordial :/ ?</div> </div> </div> </div>One way to look at it is through their interactions with the World... Gods primarily look upon and interact with the World through the lens of their Callings, Titans primarily look upon and interact with the World through their Purviews, and Primordials rarely if ever interact with the World at all.<br /> <br /> Agni is just as much an embodiment of Fire as Surtr is, but When Agni walks within the World, he is the Flame of Knowledge, the Warding Fires and the Sacrificial Conduit. When Surtr looks upon the World, he sees a nice bunch of kindling. The Primordial Svarog, doesn't do much interacting with the World at all once he built it, and indeed his next interaction is likely to be when he sweeps the whole thing aside and just builds it again.<br /> <br /> Of course since not all manifestations of a Purview are antagonistic to Humanity, you have Titans like Ao Kuang who just want to do their jobs, and since not all expressions of Callings are necessarily positive, you can have very antagonistic Gods (consider Shukra of the Devas, who explicitly mentors Titanspawn). Primordials also don't necessarily have to be on a raised power level from Gods, since Brahma is pretty explicitly the equal of Vishnu and Shiva, and I'm pretty certain Zeus could probably take on the Salmon of Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T05:49:27-08:00","id":1184707,"title":"","content":"Um I guess it's clearer. What about the Dodekatheon? Who's the Primordial if Ga\u00efa is a Titan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T06:03:18-08:00","id":1184709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184707#post1184707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um I guess it's clearer. What about the Dodekatheon? Who's the Primordial if Ga\u00efa is a Titan?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Theoi, the Primordials are likely all the Protogenoi (which you can see <a href=\"http://www.theoi.com/greek-mythology/primeval-gods.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>), which pretty much just means 'Primordial.' I don't remember Gaia being mentioned as Titan, she's sort of a perfect example of a Primordial from what I understand, but I can't for the life of me track down the Theoi preview to go double check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T06:38:58-08:00","id":1184712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184709#post1184709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the Theoi, the Primordials are likely all the Protogenoi (which you can see <a href=\"http://www.theoi.com/greek-mythology/primeval-gods.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>), which pretty much just means 'Primordial.' I don't remember Gaia being mentioned as Titan, she's sort of a perfect example of a Primordial from what I understand, but I can't for the life of me track down the Theoi preview to go double check.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> if Gaea is not a Titan, what is then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T06:41:53-08:00","id":1184714,"title":"","content":"Ouranos, Kronos, maybe Oceanos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T06:45:56-08:00","id":1184715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184712#post1184712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if Gaea is not a Titan, what is then?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Titans (Generation) are all solid examples of Titans (Game Mechanic Classification). The upper levels of Greek Cosmology is broken into three segments, the Protogenoi (Primordials), the Titans (Titans), and the Theoi (Gods). So, where Gaia is a Primordial, Atlas, Prometheus, Rhea, Cronus, Hecate, Helios, Selene, Eos, Hyperion, Idapeus, and the rest of them (you can see a pretty definitive list <a href=\"http://www.theoi.com/Titan/Titanes.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) are all Titans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T07:21:15-08:00","id":1184721,"title":"","content":"only Gaia is a Primordial? Nyx and and others before Gaia aren't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T07:45:27-08:00","id":1184728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184721#post1184721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">only Gaia is a Primordial? Nyx and and others before Gaia aren't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who even knows, until we get Heroes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T08:58:50-08:00","id":1184753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184721#post1184721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">only Gaia is a Primordial? Nyx and and others before Gaia aren't?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty certain he meant Gaia as an example and not an exhaustive list. Most of the Protogenoi, Nyx included, are Primordials by my reckoning (though I'm sure individual gaming tables will have slightly differing views as to which exact figure falls into which category). We've also been told that the status of a particular deity is not fixed... it is entirely possible for a Primordial to become a God (likely what happened to Ra) or vice versa (confirmed as to what happened to Brahma), and I'm sure God-Titan and Primordial-Titan conversion is also possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T18:35:08-08:00","id":1184972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184712#post1184712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> if Gaea is not a Titan, what is then?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Titans?<br /> <br /> Kronos, Rhea, Iapetus, Tethys, Oceanus, Theia, Hyperion, etc etc<br /> <br /> Not to mention probably Typhon and Echidna but that\u2019s a separate lineage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T18:38:46-08:00","id":1184973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1184721#post1184721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">only Gaia is a Primordial? Nyx and and others before Gaia aren't?</div> </div> </div> </div>All the Protogenoi would be Primordials<br /> <br /> Xaos - Chaos<br /> Nyx - Darkness<br /> Gaea - Earth<br /> Ouranos - Sky<br /> Pontus - Water<br /> Tartarus - Death<br /> Hemera - Sun (technically day/light, but Sun is the purview that covers that)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-12-2018, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T18:02:37-08:00","id":1185427,"title":"","content":"Guys,just a heads up. Scion:Hero is in post editing development. Which means that we're it getting it's text soon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 02-12-2018, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T18:24:04-08:00","id":1185434,"title":"","content":"I keep F5ing the backerkit page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T18:43:53-08:00","id":1185439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1185427#post1185427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys,just a heads up. Scion:Hero is in post editing development. Which means that we're it getting it's text soon!</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoo-hoo! Can't wait!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T02:57:43-08:00","id":1185526,"title":"","content":"Didnt know where to ask that but Ive never played World of Darkness but it seems like Origins sounds like WoD. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T04:51:13-08:00","id":1185542,"title":"","content":"What do you mean by &quot;like WoD?&quot;<br /> <br /> If you mean mechanically? Yeah, Storypath (what Scion uses) is very obviously a derivative of the WoD's Storyteller system.<br /> <br /> Tone and setting? They're pretty far apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T09:53:24-08:00","id":1185621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1185542#post1185542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by &quot;like WoD?&quot;<br /> <br /> If you mean mechanically? Yeah, Storypath (what Scion uses) is very obviously a derivative of the WoD's Storyteller system.<br /> <br /> Tone and setting? They're pretty far apart.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mostly meant tone because I felt that Origins was about intuitive mortals that get to meet stranger things, the paranormal. So I was wondering how different they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T13:57:45-08:00","id":1185716,"title":"","content":"Well, a huge difference regarding tone, is that in Origins, the World - the default setting - is not a world of hidden magic. The World is a place where creatures of myth and legend exist and are accepted parts of reality. It's also not a horror setting. In the WoD, people toss coins over the side of the bridge as a local quirky tradition. Nobody believes there's a troll there, but in the back of their minds they kinda know something is there and what's the harm in losing a bit of pocket change to never find out for sure? In the World, people toss coins over the side fo the bridge because there's actually a troll there, and it behaves itself as long as it gets regular offerings; nobody freaks out about this being true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T14:42:09-08:00","id":1185728,"title":"","content":"I do like that the default outlook on the creatures of legend in The World isn't the typical &quot;But that can't exist&quot;, but more &quot;That might/probably exists, but I don't want any trouble with it so I just mind my own business&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, a police chief will probably have a Scion of say, Nuada on staff, and sends him out for Weird Jobs with explicit orders of &quot;And if it IS a troll or something, make the problem go away. I really don't need the details.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T18:36:48-08:00","id":1185796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1185728#post1185728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like that the default outlook on the creatures of legend in The World isn't the typical &amp;quot;But that can't exist&amp;quot;, but more &amp;quot;That might/probably exists, but I don't want any trouble with it so I just mind my own business&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Like, a police chief will probably have a Scion of say, Nuada on staff, and sends him out for Weird Jobs with explicit orders of &amp;quot;And if it IS a troll or something, make the problem go away. I really don't need the details.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m now thinking of Orlando Jones\u2019 character on the early seasons of Sleepy Hollow. He was just so... pissed off that supernatural shot was something he had to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T19:01:37-08:00","id":1185800,"title":"","content":"Honestly I've not made it further than the setting chapter, other than a handful of dips into antagonists and storyguiding, because I just can't grasp how this world is supposed to look and feel. Multiple sections start off by saying one thing, but they end by contradicting that. &quot;Plenty of rulers and high-ranking politicians in the history of the World have claimed a divine right to leadership, and in the modern day it still happens with relative frequency.&quot; gets followed by &quot;Ultimately, the World doesn\u2019t see many more global leaders claiming divine right than our world does&quot;, which are sentences that cancel out. There are tabloids discussing different gods' shenanigans, modern pop culture is full of stuff about the gods and scions, except also the divine is mostly omens and coincidences and who even knows what's going on. It says that people take this all on a matter of faith, if not evidence, after lengthily describing how it's all anyone can talk about in the media. The gods are active, but not really, they're just not active on Earth. The supernatural is real! Amazonian is a race you can mark on a census form. Actually not really, no one really sees the supernatural, except for when they do all the time.<br /> <br /> Other sections say that all of this changes less than you might think, but I'm not convinced by what we're told here. Somewhat ironically, the proof of that claim is also a matter of faith, and it seems like this is a feature, not a bug, because the chapter starts out by telling you to suspend the disbelief and find a way to make it true (implying that it doesn't actually make much sense but now it's your job to make it fit). In storyguiding, it says that the daily lives of mortals see the divine relegated to signs and omens that may or may not be real. After we've already been told there's no such thing as coincidences and it's all true. This game can't make up its mind if it wants to be Bright or World of Darkness, and I'd really appreciate it if it would pick one.<br /> <br /> Also, I can't pronounce, like, half of the names in this book. I can read them if I use google and am familiar with IPA notation and I can guarantee you many, many players aren't going to have the willingness or familiarity to do either. Pronunciation suggestions are a must.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T20:25:47-08:00","id":1185816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1185800#post1185800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I've not made it further than the setting chapter, other than a handful of dips into antagonists and storyguiding, because I just can't grasp how this world is supposed to look and feel. Multiple sections start off by saying one thing, but they end by contradicting that. &quot;Plenty of rulers and high-ranking politicians in the history of the World have claimed a divine right to leadership, and in the modern day it still happens with relative frequency.&quot; gets followed by &quot;Ultimately, the World doesn\u2019t see many more global leaders claiming divine right than our world does&quot;, which are sentences that cancel out. There are tabloids discussing different gods' shenanigans, modern pop culture is full of stuff about the gods and scions, except also the divine is mostly omens and coincidences and who even knows what's going on. It says that people take this all on a matter of faith, if not evidence, after lengthily describing how it's all anyone can talk about in the media. The gods are active, but not really, they're just not active on Earth. The supernatural is real! Amazonian is a race you can mark on a census form. Actually not really, no one really sees the supernatural, except for when they do all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine it's a bit like how celebrity culture is nowadays. Tabloids and pop-culture are full of stuff about the daily lives of various actors and musicians, and it's literally the only thing some people know how to talk about, but the average person never meets a celebrity in their life. People in the World know full well that Gods and the supernatural are real, regardless of not usually seeing it face to face. They take it on faith the same way we take it on faith that anything else we see in the news isn't a complete fiction. And just like ours I'm sure the World has it's share of conspiracy nuts who think the Gods are actually space lizards trying to take over the world.<br /> <br /> Also, those sentences about divine right only cancel out if there aren't any leaders doing that in our world, and I'm pretty sure there still are. Possibly more than one might think. Together they mean it happens more there than here, just not by a very wide margin, or nearly so much as it used to in either case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other sections say that all of this changes less than you might think, but I'm not convinced by what we're told here. Somewhat ironically, the proof of that claim is also a matter of faith, and it seems like this is a feature, not a bug, because the chapter starts out by telling you to suspend the disbelief and find a way to make it true (implying that it doesn't actually make much sense but now it's your job to make it fit). In storyguiding, it says that the daily lives of mortals see the divine relegated to signs and omens that may or may not be real. After we've already been told there's no such thing as coincidences and it's all true. This game can't make up its mind if it wants to be Bright or World of Darkness, and I'd really appreciate it if it would pick one. </div> </div> </div>I don't think it wants to be either, but rather somewhere in between. That first part isn't saying &quot;this does't make sense so you figure it out&quot; it's saying &quot;despite our best efforts, we can't possibly make a perfectly consistent alternate history, let alone fit it in this book. When you inevitably find a piece that seems like it doesn't quite fit, rather than just pointing out the plothole and/or letting it ruin your enjoyment, try playing a round of 'How can that be true?' instead.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I can't pronounce, like, half of the names in this book. I can read them if I use google and am familiar with IPA notation and I can guarantee you many, many players aren't going to have the willingness or familiarity to do either. Pronunciation suggestions are a must. </div> </div> </div>Here I agree with you wholeheartedly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","user":"MalicWanderer","date":". 02-13-2018, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T21:13:36-08:00","id":1185825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1185800#post1185800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &amp;quot;Plenty of rulers and high-ranking politicians in the history of the World have claimed a divine right to leadership, and in the modern day it still happens with relative frequency.&amp;quot; gets followed by &amp;quot;Ultimately, the World doesn\u2019t see many more global leaders claiming divine right than our world does&amp;quot;, which are sentences that cancel out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Former US President Bush once said he felt like God wanted him to be President.<br /> <br /> People in this world invoke the divine to claim legitimacy to claims and their causes. The main difference between our world and The World is that they have more names to actively invoke.<br /> <br /> That section also, I believe, leaves it vague as to how many of these claims are true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T00:57:19-08:00","id":1185848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1185825#post1185825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Former US President Bush once said he felt like God wanted him to be President.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I have actually seen cases of supporters of both Bush and the current President use their respective defeats in the popular vote as proof that there was divine intervention to make them President instead!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T15:45:33-08:00","id":1186107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1185800#post1185800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other sections say that all of this changes less than you might think, but I'm not convinced by what we're told here. Somewhat ironically, the proof of that claim is also a matter of faith, and it seems like this is a feature, not a bug, because the chapter starts out by telling you to suspend the disbelief and find a way to make it true (implying that it doesn't actually make much sense but now it's your job to make it fit). In storyguiding, it says that the daily lives of mortals see the divine relegated to signs and omens that may or may not be real. After we've already been told there's no such thing as coincidences and it's all true. This game can't make up its mind if it wants to be Bright or World of Darkness, and I'd really appreciate it if it would pick one.</div> </div> </div> </div>How I view it is just that more people hold folklore true in the World alongside more diverse religions. I can't imagine a lot of people irl who believe extremely strongly in angels wouldn't lose their damned minds if a burning wheel lined with eyes knocked at their front door in the morning. I just apply this to the World. Someone wears a tiny image of Mjolnir and definitely believes in trolls (in the abstract), but if the Gods themselves appeared to them in a Visitation or a werewolf just exploded through the wall of a restaurant they'd barely be able to process what happens. Instead, it is signs and omens they see in the world and contextualize through their religious beliefs. See an image of a hanged man, process that through religious understanding of Odin, and maybe decide you should be extra careful that day. Thank the gods for the little things, and pray hard with a small sacrifice that night. <br /> <br /> I don't necessarily think that is how it is meant to be read, but its the best way I can grok the idea of the myths being more accepted as true vs. it still being a distant thing of omen and mystery and things you take on faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T19:33:09-08:00","id":1186155,"title":"","content":"Well, one thing that is likely is that this kind of expert is more common in the World than here...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimages.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://s14.postimg.org/ve3pk5j0x/sex-elf.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T19:37:42-08:00","id":1186156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1186107#post1186107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How I view it is just that more people hold folklore true in the World alongside more diverse religions. I can't imagine a lot of people irl who believe extremely strongly in angels wouldn't lose their damned minds if a burning wheel lined with eyes knocked at their front door in the morning. I just apply this to the World. Someone wears a tiny image of Mjolnir and definitely believes in trolls (in the abstract), but if the Gods themselves appeared to them in a Visitation or a werewolf just exploded through the wall of a restaurant they'd barely be able to process what happens. Instead, it is signs and omens they see in the world and contextualize through their religious beliefs. See an image of a hanged man, process that through religious understanding of Odin, and maybe decide you should be extra careful that day. Thank the gods for the little things, and pray hard with a small sacrifice that night.<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily think that is how it is meant to be read, but its the best way I can grok the idea of the myths being more accepted as true vs. it still being a distant thing of omen and mystery and things you take on faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see it like this. Organized crime exists, most people will not have met a member of the mob, or if they did they didn't realize it. Same thing with kitsune and Fae. They are out there, somewhere, but unless you go looking or happen to live in the right place it doesn't effect you directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T09:44:28-08:00","id":1187303,"title":"","content":"So, in light of the Crafting Rules, does the Celestial Artifice Boon in the earlier previewed Forge Purview make it possible for Heroes to create Tier 3 Items (by bringing the project down to Tier 2) or does it just mean that Heroes can build Tier 2 Items with the ease of Tier 1, and you still can't create Items that would be naturally out of your reach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T12:22:55-08:00","id":1187618,"title":"","content":"Ok, I\u2019ve tried really hard and some things are simply just escaping me. I\u2019m not sure if I missed them in the text, or if the text doesn\u2019t have them.<br /> <br /> 1) Little Mao doesn\u2019t seem to follow a lot of the creation rules. First, when he\u2019s picking his skills, he picks Culture for all three Paths, despite the rule right above the example stating that a skill can only be chosen as part of a path twice. Second, when he\u2019s distributing his attribute dots, the total dots he distributes doesn\u2019t count up to the number of attributes he\u2019s supposed to have. Thirdly, when they show him spending EXP, what he buys with 10 experience points, according to the advancement table, should cost him 65.<br /> <br /> 2) Do Paths have ratings? The text talks in places about regaining a rating, or rolling a rating, or as ratings go up, but it doesn\u2019t give any indication as to what the ratings are, how one gains ratings in Paths, or what your path Ratings start at. It also says something about rolling your Path for more dots, but there\u2019s no explanation as to what those dots are or do.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve got more, but I don\u2019t want to pile on and seem like I\u2019m being negative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8985-gnomeborg","name":"Gnomeborg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T12:26:44-08:00","id":1187621,"title":"","content":"Those have been errata'd out of the text.<br /> <br /> I cant give the specifics of ATM though<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T08:53:00-08:00","id":1188185,"title":"","content":"So, plan on raising my pledge on backerkit up to get the PDFs, which tier would that be? (pledged 25 before and only got 1st eds stuff)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1268-cosmic-mind","name":"Cosmic Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1268_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T19:00:05-08:00","id":1188367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomeborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1187618#post1187618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I\u2019ve tried really hard and some things are simply just escaping me. I\u2019m not sure if I missed them in the text, or if the text doesn\u2019t have them.<br /> <br /> 1) Little Mao doesn\u2019t seem to follow a lot of the creation rules. First, when he\u2019s picking his skills, he picks Culture for all three Paths, despite the rule right above the example stating that a skill can only be chosen as part of a path twice. Second, when he\u2019s distributing his attribute dots, the total dots he distributes doesn\u2019t count up to the number of attributes he\u2019s supposed to have. Thirdly, when they show him spending EXP, what he buys with 10 experience points, according to the advancement table, should cost him 65.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's my bad. It's earmarked for a fix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Do Paths have ratings? The text talks in places about regaining a rating, or rolling a rating, or as ratings go up, but it doesn\u2019t give any indication as to what the ratings are, how one gains ratings in Paths, or what your path Ratings start at. It also says something about rolling your Path for more dots, but there\u2019s no explanation as to what those dots are or do.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve got more, but I don\u2019t want to pile on and seem like I\u2019m being negative. </div> </div> </div>Paths in Trinity have ratings, Paths in Scion do not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T22:02:42-08:00","id":1188406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1188367#post1188367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's my bad. It's earmarked for a fix.<br /> <br /> <br /> Paths in Trinity have ratings, Paths in Scion do not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I noticed a Lover knack (On Your Side) that also references to the rating (dots) of a calling. It doesn't seem like calling are supposed to have dots either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T02:17:26-08:00","id":1188438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1188406#post1188406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea, I noticed a Lover knack (On Your Side) that also references to the rating (dots) of a calling. It doesn't seem like calling are supposed to have dots either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Callings actually are supposed to have ratings, since they help determine how many Knacks you can have active at a time. Also they figure into Clash of Wills rolls. But I think a better clarification that at Origins level your Calling level is one (I'm actually almost certain this does exist somewhere in the text, I just can't remember where, so maybe make it a little more obvious) might be good.<br /> <br /> Also, Flawlessly Platonic Ideal and Master of Arms/Weapons in Creator and Warrior respectively reference Calling ratings too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T03:16:37-08:00","id":1188446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1188406#post1188406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea, I noticed a Lover knack (On Your Side) that also references to the rating (dots) of a calling. It doesn't seem like calling are supposed to have dots either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Callings <i>do </i>have ratings. There should be a note in there that you have a phantom Calling rating of 1.<br /> <br /> Effectively there's a lot of mechanics in Scion/Trinity that deal with ratings of a Path; I just attach Callings to Path and use the mechanics to work off those (you can lose dots in a Calling through Fatebinding, for example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T06:20:03-08:00","id":1188480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1188446#post1188446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Callings <i>do </i>have ratings. There should be a note in there that you have a phantom Calling rating of 1.<br /> <br /> Effectively there's a lot of mechanics in Scion/Trinity that deal with ratings of a Path; I just attach Callings to Path and use the mechanics to work off those (you can lose dots in a Calling through Fatebinding, for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I clearly missed that. Thanks for the clarification. So you are essentially saying that all the mechanics that generally work off paths in Trinity will work off callings in Scion?<br /> <br /> How do you actually increase your calling ratings? I guess I figured they were not ratings because I didn't see them listed in the advancement section. (although I guess I could chalk that up to the fact that Origin level characters can't increase their callings and only have 1 dot) Is it going to play out similar to legend where they increase when narratively appropriate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T13:43:34-08:00","id":1188642,"title":"","content":"So, I think it was mentioned in an earlier post that each Calling has seven Mortal Knacks and five Immortal Knacks... but Guardian and Leader seem to only have six (unless I'm really missing something). Will those two be in Hero or did you just decide that a fixed same number for all Callings didn't make sense? Also, since Creator and Hunter call out how they're powers extend to non-traditional avenues of creating and hunting, could we assume that Sage Knacks deal with information in a more generalized way too? Like, could Speed Reading be used to absorb the contents of a documentary video at 50x normal playing speed instead of just reading?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T16:33:25-08:00","id":1188700,"title":"","content":"Can we get clarification on how Contacts work, dotwise and how often they can be used?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T10:36:12-08:00","id":1189625,"title":"","content":"So, more Knack Questions :<br /> <br /> 1. I'm sure this is mentioned somewhere, but I can't for the life of me find it... what kind of action is activating a Knack? I can imagine that a lot of the free Knacks probably activate whenever they're applicable, but what about Knacks that cost Momentum?<br /> <br /> 2. A number of Guardian Knacks mention your charge, and the 'A Sentinel' Knack lets you choose a charge... so do the other Knacks that mention charges only work off of the target of the 'A Sentinel' Knack (in which case you can't use those effects at Origins level since you can never have both 'A Sentinel' and the other Knack active at the same time) or does any person/group of people you choose to defend become your charge, and 'A Sentinel' only gives you the additional Enhancement? Similar queries for Judges and their cases and Hunters and their quarries.<br /> <br /> 3. I'm assuming the Swift Bandaging stunt for Doctor's Kit is supposed to say -2 Injury, since otherwise Ice Pack does everything it does and more for cheaper.<br /> <br /> 4. So, there's a bunch of Knack given Stunts (like Snare from Most Dangerous Prey) that say 'any successes above Defense'... I'm assuming that the number of successes you have in excess doesn't really matter since none of them seem to actually use the number in any concrete way... so, say I have 3 successes left over in excess of my enemy's Defense after I get all the other stunts I want... can I use both Snare and Terrify on them? Or only one? Or up to three? Basically how many of these Stunts can be bought at once given that they don't have any cost in successes listed.<br /> <br /> 5. How long do Cloak of Dread and Captain of Industry last?<br /> <br /> 6. Unerring Delivery states that you &quot;Send a message via another person \u2014 a stranger you choose on the street, a spirit or ghost of your pantheon, etc. \u2014 to someone in an instant&quot; ... does this mean that you pick a random person on the street near you who instantly teleports to the target of your message and delivers the message, or rather that any random individual <i>near the target</i> just spouts out the message to them spontaneously (and if no one is around a ghost or spirit or other power transmits the message)? I'm actually hoping for the latter, since that seems more in keeping with the mysterious fell of Liminal in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 02-26-2018, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T14:20:20-08:00","id":1189692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1189625#post1189625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or rather that any random individual <i>near the target</i> just spouts out the message to them spontaneously (and if no one is around a ghost or spirit or other power transmits the message)? I'm actually hoping for the latter, since that seems more in keeping with the mysterious fell of Liminal in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine, you're standing in line at McDonald's, and suddenly the guy behind you jerks and goes &quot;Hey, Stacy said that she's tied up and needs you to call Frank&quot; and then blinks a few times and has NO recollection of what the fuck they just said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T17:16:49-08:00","id":1189727,"title":"","content":"So if damage is dealt as a stunt, what happens if you attack someone and get successes equal to their defense? Is it just a success that doesn't do anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2472-trebius","name":"trebius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T20:43:50-08:00","id":1189758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trebius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1189727#post1189727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if damage is dealt as a stunt, what happens if you attack someone and get successes equal to their defense? Is it just a success that doesn't do anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I've seen mentioned in Origins in many places that in the case of an attack roll, ties favor the defender. Exactly because you need to inflict wounds as a Stunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T10:49:11-07:00","id":1194888,"title":"","content":"Hero Is Out!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2472-trebius","name":"trebius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T12:32:51-07:00","id":1194932,"title":"","content":"Is there gonna be a thread for reporting errors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T12:52:23-07:00","id":1194941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1194932#post1194932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there gonna be a thread for reporting errors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not for this, but when the backer PDF goes out, as per the message on the Digital Downloads page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T12:55:33-07:00","id":1194943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1194932#post1194932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there gonna be a thread for reporting errors?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure someone will make one. I noticed a few points while putting in bookmarks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 03-13-2018, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T13:00:20-07:00","id":1194947,"title":"","content":"Praise the sun! Time to slack off at work and skim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T00:40:50-07:00","id":1196735,"title":"","content":"A few things on Favored Approaches:<ul><li>The Hero attribute generation ordering (assign Favored points, then Arena) is cleaner than Origins since it doesn't involve overflow</li> <li>Do they do anything after character creation?</li> <li>When you spend XP to change it, does that just move attribute points around? This will lead to identical characters that spent different XP to get there, and can be accomplished with 1-point shifting over time. So, I'll probably houserule that players get this back over time (e.g., +3 XP/session for 5 sessions)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18839-zilaenor","name":"zilaenor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}